1
00:00:03,550 --> 00:02:03,550
Please contact us for any inquiries
turkision@gmail.com

2
00:02:04,085 --> 00:02:08,630
No living creature was harmed during the
filming of this series

3
00:02:11,985 --> 00:02:13,985
We defeated the enemy, son.

4
00:02:14,285 --> 00:02:16,915
They will attack us now.

5
00:02:17,145 --> 00:02:18,835
For this reason, you will grow up.

6
00:02:18,975 --> 00:02:22,255
You will grow so that the oppressed
may rest in our shadows.

7
00:02:22,305 --> 00:02:24,095
You will get strong.

8
00:02:24,475 --> 00:02:26,215
You have no other solution.

9
00:02:32,155 --> 00:02:34,025
You're wasting your power in vain.

10
00:02:42,155 --> 00:02:46,265
If you waste your strength like this, you
won't have the strength to defend.

11
00:02:46,345 --> 00:02:47,725
Come on, get up.

12
00:02:51,805 --> 00:02:54,415
You say my power ends
quickly, huh, Osman Bey?

13
00:02:54,885 --> 00:02:57,415
It must be because of my weakness.

14
00:02:57,485 --> 00:03:00,545
So, you will continue to defend
while you are on the ground.

15
00:03:02,695 --> 00:03:04,255
Come up.

16
00:03:12,525 --> 00:03:13,875
Son.

17
00:03:13,965 --> 00:03:15,525
Give me your hand.

18
00:03:19,425 --> 00:03:21,175
Come on, son.

19
00:03:21,375 --> 00:03:22,915
Come on.

20
00:03:24,915 --> 00:03:26,675
Your training is over.

21
00:03:26,895 --> 00:03:28,465
Go and continue teaching.

22
00:03:39,275 --> 00:03:40,765
Aladdin.

23
00:03:40,865 --> 00:03:42,215
Come on, son.

24
00:03:43,585 --> 00:03:44,915
Come on.

25
00:03:45,225 --> 00:03:47,005
Come on, Aladdin.

26
00:03:56,035 --> 00:03:57,595
Bala.

27
00:03:59,345 --> 00:04:00,665
My Bey.

28
00:04:04,315 --> 00:04:06,465
This pressure is enough for my son.

29
00:04:07,155 --> 00:04:09,235
Practice with someone of your level.

30
00:04:15,325 --> 00:04:17,185
Are you of my level?

31
00:04:26,145 --> 00:04:29,345
The level becomes clear during the fight, Osman Bey.

32
00:04:32,475 --> 00:04:34,035
Okay, then.

33
00:04:37,265 --> 00:04:38,605
Come on.

34
00:04:50,485 --> 00:04:54,495
Your strength has not
changed, my dear Osman.

35
00:05:05,725 --> 00:05:07,285
And your beauty hasn't changed.

36
00:05:10,655 --> 00:05:12,825
It's still the same as in the past.

37
00:05:17,575 --> 00:05:19,355
Like the first day.

38
00:05:37,265 --> 00:05:38,645
My Bey.

39
00:05:40,355 --> 00:05:43,085
It's Hasan, the messenger who
will go to Constantinople.

40
00:05:43,815 --> 00:05:45,195
Thank yıu.

41
00:05:49,715 --> 00:05:51,245
You...

42
00:05:54,085 --> 00:05:55,955
will hand this over to the emperor.

43
00:05:57,675 --> 00:06:01,455
This dagger is evidence of
what is written in the letter.

44
00:06:01,735 --> 00:06:04,765
When you get to
Constantinople, tell Konur.

45
00:06:05,575 --> 00:06:08,815
Those who attacked us on the way will
try to attack us again.

46
00:06:08,845 --> 00:06:10,165
I'm going with two more horses...

47
00:06:10,195 --> 00:06:11,405
and helpers.

48
00:06:11,455 --> 00:06:12,935
Let the moon light my way...

49
00:06:12,955 --> 00:06:15,225
I will go without rest, my Bey.

50
00:06:15,485 --> 00:06:17,135
Thank you. Godspeed you.

51
00:06:22,735 --> 00:06:24,085
- Boran.
- Sir.

52
00:06:24,185 --> 00:06:25,635
Take extra measures.

53
00:06:25,665 --> 00:06:27,405
Send different Alps.

54
00:06:27,875 --> 00:06:29,395
The enemy is different.

55
00:06:29,945 --> 00:06:31,985
Their moves will be different.

56
00:06:32,345 --> 00:06:34,055
Your command, my Bey.

57
00:06:38,145 --> 00:06:40,375
The enemy is different, but...

58
00:06:42,115 --> 00:06:44,695
we are not the same either.

59
00:06:46,885 --> 00:06:49,435
I deserve the throne...

60
00:06:49,895 --> 00:06:51,725
and Rome deserves me.

61
00:06:52,505 --> 00:06:55,655
Osman, that idiot prevented my access to the throne.

62
00:06:56,715 --> 00:06:58,245
But he will pay the price.

63
00:06:58,365 --> 00:06:59,695
He will!

64
00:07:01,175 --> 00:07:02,885
He knew everything.

65
00:07:03,085 --> 00:07:04,825
He knew everything.

66
00:07:06,105 --> 00:07:08,535
He put a spy in my city.

67
00:07:10,195 --> 00:07:13,215
Now, I will have a spy
in Yenişehir too.

68
00:07:47,055 --> 00:07:48,365
This smell...

69
00:07:53,345 --> 00:07:55,045
This is the smell of death.

70
00:08:06,985 --> 00:08:09,005
Who are you?
What do you want?

71
00:08:10,095 --> 00:08:12,155
I have gifts for you.

72
00:08:20,375 --> 00:08:24,435
I'm Frigg, the messenger of death.

73
00:08:24,535 --> 00:08:25,955
You ignoble!

74
00:08:26,075 --> 00:08:27,615
I'll make you pay for this!

75
00:09:26,975 --> 00:09:28,805
I'm Marta.

76
00:09:29,585 --> 00:09:32,465
I've come to Yenişehir as a cloth
merchant.

77
00:09:33,255 --> 00:09:35,315
I am sure you will love me very much.

78
00:09:39,485 --> 00:09:41,035
I ask you...

79
00:09:42,455 --> 00:09:45,625
Is the price of the throne only a spy?

80
00:09:48,985 --> 00:09:51,375
No, no!

81
00:09:51,535 --> 00:09:53,065
Not like that!

82
00:09:53,825 --> 00:09:57,515
I'll take everyone around him!

83
00:09:58,895 --> 00:10:01,575
I'll take this Beys from him.

84
00:10:05,555 --> 00:10:07,825
I will create a cliff between them...

85
00:10:08,095 --> 00:10:11,115
and I will push Osman.

86
00:10:12,935 --> 00:10:18,285
He thinks he has agreed with that
cowardly and foolish emperor.

87
00:10:18,725 --> 00:10:22,365
I will tear up that agreement.

88
00:10:22,665 --> 00:10:24,535
I'll tear it up!

89
00:10:24,575 --> 00:10:27,445
Macri's website

90
00:11:25,725 --> 00:11:27,055
Is it enough?

91
00:11:27,175 --> 00:11:28,705
Not enough.

92
00:11:28,895 --> 00:11:30,485
Not enough.

93
00:11:33,805 --> 00:11:38,845
The throne would have promised power
to all the sons of Rome.

94
00:11:42,915 --> 00:11:45,465
And I will take your sons, Osman.

95
00:11:46,925 --> 00:11:48,425
First, Orhan...

96
00:11:51,415 --> 00:11:54,075
The young one will die in my hands.

97
00:11:54,485 --> 00:11:57,795
My Beys, we are going to
Sarıpınar for hunting.

98
00:11:57,835 --> 00:11:59,435
That place is dangerous, Bey.

99
00:11:59,445 --> 00:12:00,765
It's difficult for hunting.

100
00:12:00,795 --> 00:12:02,625
A good hunter does everything.

101
00:12:03,655 --> 00:12:05,225
This land is ours.

102
00:12:05,695 --> 00:12:07,165
We will know every inch of it.

103
00:12:07,235 --> 00:12:09,155
We'll know it so we don't become prey.

104
00:12:09,215 --> 00:12:11,525
It's ours no matter what.

105
00:12:11,605 --> 00:12:13,215
Let's go and hunt, my Bey.

106
00:12:15,025 --> 00:12:19,585
My Bey, you are giving them a hard test.

107
00:12:20,285 --> 00:12:21,525
What is your intention?

108
00:12:22,505 --> 00:12:24,595
You know a Bey while hunting.

109
00:12:25,125 --> 00:12:29,225
Let's put them to a hard one in distress,
so that we can rest on them in prosperity.

110
00:12:30,315 --> 00:12:32,655
Come on, may our hunt be blessed.

111
00:12:32,765 --> 00:12:34,575
Thank you.

112
00:12:34,905 --> 00:12:36,225
Come on.

113
00:12:38,445 --> 00:12:41,015
So, he goes hunting with his
Beys, doesn't he?

114
00:12:42,195 --> 00:12:43,725
Yes, sir.

115
00:12:44,265 --> 00:12:46,775
You are the prey, Orhan.

116
00:13:04,555 --> 00:13:07,135
You interfered with the fate of this city.

117
00:13:08,065 --> 00:13:11,115
And I will make you live in hell
in this world, Osman.

118
00:13:18,105 --> 00:13:19,645
As for you...

119
00:13:24,065 --> 00:13:25,565
Cardinal!

120
00:13:27,915 --> 00:13:31,485
The Papacy will be very angry when
they learn that Osman killed you.

121
00:13:32,435 --> 00:13:35,435
So, they will give me a very large army.

122
00:13:36,885 --> 00:13:40,155
I will have the throne and kill
Osman at the same time.

123
00:13:45,105 --> 00:13:46,405
So sad.

124
00:13:47,515 --> 00:13:49,015
So sad.

125
00:13:49,695 --> 00:13:51,195
So sad.

126
00:13:52,865 --> 00:13:57,875
I'm sorry for everyone who tries
to stand against me.

127
00:14:01,605 --> 00:14:03,745
- Well done, sisters.
- Thank you.

128
00:14:04,415 --> 00:14:07,685
Mashallah, what did you cook, Ülgen Hatun?

129
00:14:08,005 --> 00:14:09,895
Its scent reeks throughout the palace.

130
00:14:10,725 --> 00:14:12,725
Fill me a plate.

131
00:14:13,065 --> 00:14:14,365
No.

132
00:14:15,305 --> 00:14:19,865
Sisters, make a roll of
bread for him.

133
00:14:20,505 --> 00:14:23,225
I won't give food to anyone.
It's for Orhan Bey.

134
00:14:26,665 --> 00:14:27,885
Thank you, Ülgen Hatun.

135
00:14:28,365 --> 00:14:29,665
Thank you.

136
00:14:38,585 --> 00:14:40,645
Oh, this smell...

137
00:14:43,075 --> 00:14:46,045
Don't do that, Cerkutay.

138
00:14:47,815 --> 00:14:49,115
No...

139
00:14:49,625 --> 00:14:51,345
I can't stand it...

140
00:15:13,065 --> 00:15:14,565
Cerkutay.

141
00:15:15,895 --> 00:15:17,485
Ülgen Hatun.

142
00:15:20,565 --> 00:15:22,175
Eat, Cerguday, eat!

143
00:15:22,315 --> 00:15:23,605
Stop.

144
00:15:26,005 --> 00:15:27,795
I will give you that too.

145
00:15:36,625 --> 00:15:38,325
Here's a spoon for you.

146
00:15:47,135 --> 00:15:48,995
You weren't mad at me, were you?

147
00:15:49,775 --> 00:15:51,865
No, no, why am I even angry?

148
00:15:55,825 --> 00:15:57,445
Can I eat this food?

149
00:15:57,555 --> 00:15:58,875
Yes, eat it

150
00:16:01,335 --> 00:16:02,535
Stop.

151
00:16:02,805 --> 00:16:05,055
I'll give you bulgur (kind of rice) too.

152
00:16:09,915 --> 00:16:11,445
Enjoy it.

153
00:16:21,065 --> 00:16:22,445
Thank you, sisters!

154
00:16:24,645 --> 00:16:26,645
- You're welcome.
- Good evening.

155
00:16:30,835 --> 00:16:33,815
Eat, Cerguday, it is for you.

156
00:16:41,705 --> 00:16:45,845
Cerguday knows very well

157
00:16:46,485 --> 00:16:50,545
He knows what Orhan Bey likes. That's why
I let him eat.

158
00:16:52,245 --> 00:16:54,355
If he likes the food, Orhan Bey
will like it too.

159
00:16:57,335 --> 00:16:58,335
Ülgen!

160
00:16:59,765 --> 00:17:01,325
Oh, I'm late!

161
00:17:02,165 --> 00:17:03,445
Yes, Malhun Hatun?

162
00:17:05,253 --> 00:17:06,704
Come on, Ülgen, we're leaving.

163
00:17:06,744 --> 00:17:09,914
- Have you finished preparing the food?
- Yes, it will be ready soon, Malhun Hatun.

164
00:17:09,925 --> 00:17:11,223
Okay, then.
Come on.

165
00:17:14,575 --> 00:17:17,075
Hurry up sisters, we're late.

166
00:17:23,895 --> 00:17:26,755
- Salam Alaikum.
- Alaikum Salam.

167
00:17:28,740 --> 00:17:30,330
Dursun Fakı.

168
00:17:30,620 --> 00:17:35,540
Send messengers to Samarkand, Tabriz
and all the Turkmen tribes.

169
00:17:39,700 --> 00:17:41,200
Alps!

170
00:17:41,230 --> 00:17:43,600
Draw your swords!

171
00:17:48,280 --> 00:17:49,480
Look.

172
00:17:51,360 --> 00:17:54,630
Which one of you has a sword
sharper than your pen?

173
00:17:59,630 --> 00:18:04,170
The homeland is protected by swords,
but is run by wisdom.

174
00:18:07,170 --> 00:18:11,770
We will have students of knowledge.

175
00:18:12,390 --> 00:18:13,980
For this reason...

176
00:18:14,130 --> 00:18:17,880
Summon the mudarris (teachers).

177
00:18:18,820 --> 00:18:21,390
They are welcomed in our lands.

178
00:18:22,020 --> 00:18:24,510
This is good news, my Bey.

179
00:18:24,930 --> 00:18:29,500
When the light of conquest is seen, the
fire of science is flared up.

180
00:18:30,400 --> 00:18:34,190
This will make Yenişehir a
center of science.

181
00:18:35,090 --> 00:18:36,590
Mashallah.

182
00:18:36,810 --> 00:18:38,890
We are always looking for the future...

183
00:18:39,800 --> 00:18:41,890
but we stick to our roots.

184
00:18:43,540 --> 00:18:46,360
We dream of Yenişehir and beyond.

185
00:18:46,510 --> 00:18:49,580
But we will never forget
what is behind us.

186
00:18:51,450 --> 00:18:52,950
For this reason...

187
00:18:53,350 --> 00:18:55,910
We will now go to inspect Karacahisar.

188
00:18:56,000 --> 00:18:57,500
Your command, my Bey.

189
00:19:44,090 --> 00:19:45,970
Öktem Tent

190
00:19:57,385 --> 00:19:59,105
Oh my Allah.

191
00:20:33,765 --> 00:20:35,065
Oh...

192
00:20:38,875 --> 00:20:40,175
My mother.

193
00:20:40,515 --> 00:20:42,015
My beautiful mother.

194
00:20:44,535 --> 00:20:47,105
Batur is more than a brother to me.

195
00:20:48,915 --> 00:20:50,675
His breath is mine...

196
00:20:51,305 --> 00:20:52,835
and his soul is my soul.

197
00:20:53,605 --> 00:20:55,685
Sleep in peace, mother.

198
00:20:56,255 --> 00:20:57,835
Rest in peace.

199
00:21:13,875 --> 00:21:15,765
What's wrong with you, woman?

200
00:21:18,775 --> 00:21:20,505
I fell asleep a bit.

201
00:21:21,295 --> 00:21:23,015
And I dreamt of my mother.

202
00:21:29,905 --> 00:21:31,725
May Allah bless her.

203
00:21:31,975 --> 00:21:34,085
She was crying.

204
00:21:34,745 --> 00:21:36,075
She told me "my daughter...

205
00:21:36,155 --> 00:21:39,245
take care of your brother Batur" she said.

206
00:21:42,605 --> 00:21:44,375
- Take it.
- Thank you.

207
00:21:51,115 --> 00:21:53,965
My mother gave birth to a son.

208
00:21:55,035 --> 00:22:01,665
However, both my mother and father
left before they could embrace their son.

209
00:22:03,725 --> 00:22:05,515
And I saw Batur as my son.

210
00:22:08,295 --> 00:22:11,865
But I couldn't have a son for you.

211
00:22:14,065 --> 00:22:16,735
You gave me hope, woman, you
gave me a soul.

212
00:22:17,515 --> 00:22:18,995
She gave me Alçiçek.

213
00:22:20,505 --> 00:22:23,765
May Allah give both of you a long life.

214
00:22:25,215 --> 00:22:27,865
Also, don't you know it, woman...

215
00:22:28,615 --> 00:22:33,625
thanks to Batur, I didn't need a son.

216
00:22:35,035 --> 00:22:36,335
Tell me.

217
00:22:38,785 --> 00:22:40,285
What worries you?

218
00:22:41,715 --> 00:22:44,055
I have seen demons with horns.

219
00:22:45,435 --> 00:22:48,255
They were screaming like a black curse.

220
00:22:48,925 --> 00:22:51,485
They were dragging my brother
into a deep hole.

221
00:22:51,675 --> 00:22:53,445
Don't do this, Hatun.

222
00:22:53,485 --> 00:22:55,535
This isn't Batur's firs time leaving.

223
00:22:58,595 --> 00:22:59,895
Raise your head.

224
00:22:59,945 --> 00:23:01,665
Is this worthy of you?

225
00:23:02,005 --> 00:23:03,905
I'm not comfortable, my Bey.

226
00:23:04,365 --> 00:23:05,935
You followed Osman's orders.

227
00:23:06,915 --> 00:23:10,185
- You sent my brother.
- Don't say that, Hatun.

228
00:23:10,645 --> 00:23:14,085
Is there a limit for a hero whose
love for conquest ignites in his heart?

229
00:23:14,295 --> 00:23:16,745
The headquarters of Makri
is the gate of conquests.

230
00:23:16,825 --> 00:23:18,625
The door of the soldier is a conquest.

231
00:23:18,665 --> 00:23:20,105
And the key to that door...

232
00:23:20,125 --> 00:23:23,145
is in the hearts of Batur
and our Alps, Hatun.

233
00:23:24,965 --> 00:23:26,255
You have to understand that.

234
00:23:27,955 --> 00:23:32,445
Also, I want Batur to grow up
next to Osman Bey.

235
00:23:33,325 --> 00:23:37,095
So that he will be in the right place.

236
00:23:39,635 --> 00:23:42,225
He would be good Bey, wouldn't he?

237
00:23:43,295 --> 00:23:46,035
Of course!

238
00:23:47,195 --> 00:23:51,015
I know, Hatun, Batur will do
this job properly.

239
00:23:53,285 --> 00:23:54,485
Look...

240
00:23:56,275 --> 00:23:57,975
When the time comes...

241
00:23:58,115 --> 00:24:02,535
When the death comes for me...

242
00:24:02,785 --> 00:24:04,645
May Allah give you a long life, my Bey!

243
00:24:05,005 --> 00:24:06,385
Then...

244
00:24:07,235 --> 00:24:09,285
Batur will sit on that chair.

245
00:24:10,725 --> 00:24:12,055
Inshallah...

246
00:24:12,125 --> 00:24:13,525
with Osman Bey...

247
00:24:13,805 --> 00:24:19,185
He will be a soldier in the country that
will rule the whole world!

248
00:24:20,595 --> 00:24:22,705
Don't worry.

249
00:24:24,005 --> 00:24:25,355
Don't worry.

250
00:24:32,375 --> 00:24:34,135
Makri

251
00:24:44,085 --> 00:24:45,585
What happened here?

252
00:24:52,835 --> 00:24:54,355
Alps!

253
00:24:55,065 --> 00:24:56,585
Be careful!

254
00:25:00,820 --> 00:25:02,410
If we hadn't seen the smoke...

255
00:25:02,900 --> 00:25:04,790
we wouldn't know there was a massacre.

256
00:25:05,630 --> 00:25:07,640
Are these the measures you have taken?

257
00:25:07,740 --> 00:25:09,540
We couldn't do our job!

258
00:25:10,160 --> 00:25:12,280
We did not prevent
the killing of people.

259
00:25:13,920 --> 00:25:16,430
Osman Bey was right.

260
00:25:39,770 --> 00:25:41,070
Who are you?

261
00:25:44,710 --> 00:25:46,210
I am Olof.

262
00:25:46,620 --> 00:25:48,660
Turks' executioner!

263
00:25:50,650 --> 00:25:52,030
Alps!

264
00:25:52,120 --> 00:25:53,640
If we die, we are martyrs.

265
00:25:53,720 --> 00:25:55,470
And if we live, we are Ghazis.

266
00:25:55,530 --> 00:25:59,620
Allah is great! Allah is great!

267
00:25:59,650 --> 00:26:01,010
Attack!

268
00:26:37,185 --> 00:26:39,445
Little Orhan.

269
00:26:40,415 --> 00:26:42,295
Think of yourself as a hunter.

270
00:26:42,525 --> 00:26:44,085
Let's attack, sir.

271
00:26:44,115 --> 00:26:46,635
Wait! Not yet.

272
00:26:48,625 --> 00:26:53,465
He will fall into our hands
while it hunts its prey.

273
00:26:54,535 --> 00:26:58,045
- Did you kill those next to the horses?
- They're all dead, sir.

274
00:28:04,755 --> 00:28:06,615
Mashallah.

275
00:28:27,855 --> 00:28:29,465
Now!

276
00:28:30,535 --> 00:28:31,725
My Bey.

277
00:28:33,425 --> 00:28:35,185
Alps!
Attack!

278
00:28:48,135 --> 00:28:50,915
My Bey! We have to get you out of here.

279
00:28:50,955 --> 00:28:52,565
I will not leave my Alps alone.

280
00:28:52,635 --> 00:28:53,855
Allah is eternal!

281
00:28:53,895 --> 00:28:55,615
Allah is eternal!

282
00:28:56,705 --> 00:29:00,045
Allah is eternal!

283
00:29:45,395 --> 00:29:47,635
I came to get you, little boy.

284
00:29:47,725 --> 00:29:50,395
Whoever tries to hurt me is hurt first.

285
00:30:08,155 --> 00:30:09,695
You ignoble!

286
00:30:14,875 --> 00:30:16,055
My Bey.

287
00:30:16,715 --> 00:30:17,715
My Bey.

288
00:30:23,825 --> 00:30:25,845
I will kill you.

289
00:30:30,775 --> 00:30:31,795
My Bey.

290
00:30:32,105 --> 00:30:34,895
But slowly...

291
00:30:44,295 --> 00:30:45,885
You won't get away with it.

292
00:30:46,065 --> 00:30:48,235
I'll tear you apart.

293
00:30:49,495 --> 00:30:52,105
You won't even have a grave.

294
00:30:54,085 --> 00:30:57,845
Osman will beg me to find your remains.

295
00:31:12,365 --> 00:31:13,715
Alps!

296
00:31:13,915 --> 00:31:16,095
Take your places.

297
00:31:19,385 --> 00:31:22,225
Look around
to find out who did this.

298
00:31:37,955 --> 00:31:41,545
"We belong to Allah and to
Him we shall return."

299
00:31:54,585 --> 00:31:56,445
This...

300
00:32:01,365 --> 00:32:02,755
My Bey.

301
00:32:03,425 --> 00:32:06,345
The martyrs are the Alps of Orhan Bey.

302
00:32:06,735 --> 00:32:09,705
- Track them down.
- Your command, my Sir.

303
00:32:13,025 --> 00:32:14,615
Orhan.

304
00:32:15,095 --> 00:32:16,565
My Orhan.

305
00:32:16,625 --> 00:32:17,935
Gölge.

306
00:32:24,245 --> 00:32:26,325
- Ayaz.
- Yes, Bey.

307
00:32:26,595 --> 00:32:28,095
Take the flag

308
00:32:28,485 --> 00:32:31,775
You go to Karacahisar
and we will follow their tracks.

309
00:32:32,015 --> 00:32:33,735
Your command, my Bey.

310
00:32:40,655 --> 00:32:46,375
If my son is hurt, I swear that
I will burn this world!

311
00:32:46,475 --> 00:32:47,845
My Bey.

312
00:32:49,405 --> 00:32:51,225
This way.

313
00:32:51,295 --> 00:32:54,655
- Osman.
- Don't worry.

314
00:32:54,905 --> 00:32:57,435
Orhan Bey won't be under
the control of the infidels.

315
00:32:57,465 --> 00:32:58,845
Come on.

316
00:33:08,425 --> 00:33:11,965
We have to search the chests.
Open these chests

317
00:33:12,955 --> 00:33:14,315
Open.

318
00:33:16,885 --> 00:33:18,945
These chests will not be opened.

319
00:33:23,645 --> 00:33:27,115
I can't let you into town
without checking all the boxes. (chests)

320
00:33:29,715 --> 00:33:31,195
Alps!

321
00:33:37,705 --> 00:33:38,955
What's going on?

322
00:33:38,995 --> 00:33:41,875
They don't let us open the chests.

323
00:33:45,945 --> 00:33:47,375
Open the chests.

324
00:33:53,105 --> 00:33:54,645
Stop.

325
00:33:56,485 --> 00:33:58,605
These boxes are gifts to Osman Bey.

326
00:34:00,515 --> 00:34:03,295
It was specially brought by
my brother Leo.

327
00:34:06,955 --> 00:34:08,764
Who are you?

328
00:34:09,074 --> 00:34:11,205
How dare you ask for this?

329
00:34:11,745 --> 00:34:16,245
I'm Osman Bey's wife.
Bala Hatun.

330
00:34:18,804 --> 00:34:21,195
So, you're Leo's sister...

331
00:34:22,295 --> 00:34:24,085
Tell me what's your name.

332
00:34:26,675 --> 00:34:28,465
Forgive me for being so bold.

333
00:34:29,355 --> 00:34:33,435
You look like an important woman
but I couldn't tell who you are.

334
00:34:35,235 --> 00:34:37,525
My name is Marta.

335
00:34:39,614 --> 00:34:41,114
Marta.

336
00:34:48,915 --> 00:34:50,505
It doesn't matter.

337
00:34:51,175 --> 00:34:53,235
The gifts are so beautiful, Marta.

338
00:34:55,164 --> 00:34:57,755
Mr. Leo's shop is on this side.

339
00:35:00,465 --> 00:35:01,845
Marta.

340
00:35:02,055 --> 00:35:04,165
- My beautiful sister.
- My brother.

341
00:35:08,415 --> 00:35:10,385
It seems you have met Bala Hatun.

342
00:35:14,575 --> 00:35:18,215
Thank you for the gifts, Marta, but...

343
00:35:23,715 --> 00:35:25,905
it seems like Mr. Leo didn't
tell you anything.

344
00:35:29,985 --> 00:35:34,155
Osman Bey doesn't take gifts from
merchants and pays for them.

345
00:35:37,475 --> 00:35:40,595
Okay then, Bala Hatun.

346
00:35:43,245 --> 00:35:47,195
- Okay, then! Welcome.
- Thank you.

347
00:35:54,945 --> 00:35:56,475
Bala.

348
00:35:57,775 --> 00:35:59,605
Bala Hatun.

349
00:36:01,625 --> 00:36:03,765
Osman Bey's dear love.

350
00:36:04,245 --> 00:36:11,105
Now you know Marta.
You will meet Frigg when you die.

351
00:36:16,475 --> 00:36:18,245
Carry him.

352
00:36:28,385 --> 00:36:30,505
Do you think you will live anymore?

353
00:36:30,865 --> 00:36:33,395
If I wanted to, I would cut
off your head now.

354
00:36:37,945 --> 00:36:39,525
I will cut it already.

355
00:36:40,835 --> 00:36:43,655
But death will not be so easy
for you.

356
00:37:05,015 --> 00:37:06,805
Osman's son.

357
00:37:07,845 --> 00:37:09,895
You're basically dead.

358
00:37:12,225 --> 00:37:15,135
And I'm the demon that's going
to cut you to pieces.

359
00:38:20,465 --> 00:38:22,035
His father has come.

360
00:38:23,915 --> 00:38:25,505
Tell me.

361
00:38:25,575 --> 00:38:27,925
It wuld be your turn after your son.

362
00:38:28,445 --> 00:38:30,305
But I can start with you.

363
00:38:30,535 --> 00:38:33,035
We got you, my Orhan.

364
00:39:07,515 --> 00:39:08,825
Brother!

365
00:39:09,115 --> 00:39:10,335
Brother!

366
00:39:10,375 --> 00:39:12,075
You will be fine, my lion.

367
00:40:24,115 --> 00:40:25,495
Stand up.

368
00:40:27,915 --> 00:40:30,335
Do you think that what you did
will be unpunished?

369
00:40:30,395 --> 00:40:32,145
Go back to your village.

370
00:40:34,195 --> 00:40:36,205
You killed innocents.

371
00:40:36,965 --> 00:40:39,045
You stole the gold we collected.

372
00:40:39,685 --> 00:40:42,275
We punished you.

373
00:40:55,465 --> 00:40:56,775
Stand him up.

374
00:42:01,385 --> 00:42:02,955
Orhan!

375
00:42:09,475 --> 00:42:11,065
Orhan!

376
00:42:11,115 --> 00:42:12,485
My son.

377
00:42:12,485 --> 00:42:14,075
I got you, I got you, son.

378
00:42:14,125 --> 00:42:15,825
I got you, Orhan, I got you.

379
00:42:17,975 --> 00:42:19,305
My son.

380
00:42:40,475 --> 00:42:41,775
Olof.

381
00:42:45,645 --> 00:42:47,235
The Turks are coming.

382
00:42:48,205 --> 00:42:50,195
I was waiting for them.

383
00:42:56,995 --> 00:42:58,515
Let them come and...

384
00:42:59,255 --> 00:43:01,985
see this massacre they caused.

385
00:43:18,115 --> 00:43:20,805
Hang on, my Orhan.

386
00:43:32,015 --> 00:43:33,325
My son.

387
00:43:49,445 --> 00:43:51,145
When we bury our martyrs...

388
00:43:51,595 --> 00:43:53,305
you will be buried.

389
00:43:53,385 --> 00:43:54,725
Look at me.

390
00:43:54,745 --> 00:43:57,005
Before you pay for what've you done...

391
00:43:57,335 --> 00:43:59,285
even the soil is forbidden for you.

392
00:44:00,645 --> 00:44:02,855
The soil is worthy of you helpless ones.

393
00:44:03,185 --> 00:44:05,465
As for us, what is
worthy of us is Valhalla.

394
00:44:05,745 --> 00:44:08,475
You tried to kill my son.

395
00:44:09,875 --> 00:44:12,515
I protected him from my eyes
in a silk swaddling gown!

396
00:44:12,585 --> 00:44:14,725
You will die in pain.

397
00:44:14,965 --> 00:44:18,475
Death is at your door.

398
00:44:18,595 --> 00:44:20,565
You will all die.

399
00:44:32,175 --> 00:44:36,485
Whoever touches my son or touches us...

400
00:44:36,875 --> 00:44:38,875
will pay for it dearly.

401
00:44:44,085 --> 00:44:48,265
You touch my son Orhan, right?

402
00:44:49,635 --> 00:44:51,135
I will kill you.

403
00:45:16,725 --> 00:45:19,375
So,you broke my son's fingers.

404
00:45:22,095 --> 00:45:26,975
I'll cut off your fingers.

405
00:45:28,565 --> 00:45:30,775
You will never be able to
hold the sword again.

406
00:45:31,855 --> 00:45:34,425
You will never be able to
harm an innocent person.

407
00:45:38,850 --> 00:45:40,590
My son, huh?

408
00:45:46,185 --> 00:45:47,755
What is broken heals...

409
00:45:50,515 --> 00:45:52,215
Well, what about cuts?

410
00:46:09,385 --> 00:46:13,665
Scream.

411
00:46:20,885 --> 00:46:25,945
In my lands, only the voices of
the oppressed are heard.

412
00:46:27,175 --> 00:46:29,885
No one will hear...

413
00:46:30,625 --> 00:46:32,485
your voice.

414
00:46:34,265 --> 00:46:35,975
Scream if you want.

415
00:46:40,095 --> 00:46:42,365
No one will hear you.

416
00:47:15,325 --> 00:47:17,415
What happened here, Öktem Bey?

417
00:47:26,255 --> 00:47:27,565
My Alps.

418
00:47:32,825 --> 00:47:34,345
Batur.

419
00:47:36,375 --> 00:47:37,695
Be careful.

420
00:47:59,995 --> 00:48:01,345
Alps.

421
00:48:40,915 --> 00:48:42,895
Are you here to take your revenge?

422
00:48:42,925 --> 00:48:45,245
If you did this to my Alps...

423
00:48:45,345 --> 00:48:47,435
I came to kill you.

424
00:48:51,325 --> 00:48:55,875
Are you the one who gave these
corpses the order to raid the village?

425
00:48:55,955 --> 00:48:58,915
What's the matter, you
ignoble dog?

426
00:48:58,975 --> 00:49:00,935
Are you the one who
gave them the order?

427
00:49:00,975 --> 00:49:03,315
Öktem Bey is clearly not aware of it.

428
00:49:04,155 --> 00:49:06,245
Put down your swords and let's talk.

429
00:49:09,325 --> 00:49:11,775
It's too late to talk.

430
00:49:12,065 --> 00:49:14,555
This is the time for revenge, Bayındır
Bey.

431
00:49:15,415 --> 00:49:18,665
So, there is nothing for us to do.

432
00:49:19,305 --> 00:49:21,165
Our swords will speak.

433
00:49:27,985 --> 00:49:29,515
Öktem Bey!

434
00:49:29,975 --> 00:49:31,345
Stop.

435
00:49:32,785 --> 00:49:35,175
You draw your sword before
you take the command...

436
00:49:35,245 --> 00:49:37,245
it means you kill yourself first, don't.

437
00:49:38,575 --> 00:49:44,495
My command is the tears of the
mothers of these martyrs, Turgut!

438
00:49:44,715 --> 00:49:46,945
Will I have mercy on these?

439
00:49:46,945 --> 00:49:49,705
How do I have mercy on these, Turgut Bey?

440
00:49:50,665 --> 00:49:51,965
Alps!

441
00:49:56,585 --> 00:49:58,165
Öktem Bey!

442
00:49:58,265 --> 00:49:59,855
Öktem Bey!

443
00:50:00,795 --> 00:50:03,135
Where did you hear that we leave
without revenge?

444
00:50:03,165 --> 00:50:04,925
That we have mercy on who did that?

445
00:50:04,985 --> 00:50:06,205
Where did you hear that?

446
00:50:06,225 --> 00:50:08,015
Be patient, Öktem Bey!

447
00:50:16,905 --> 00:50:18,755
Let's understand
what happened first.

448
00:50:18,775 --> 00:50:22,595
And when it's time for revenge,
I swear I'll be by your side.

449
00:50:24,605 --> 00:50:25,925
Be patient.

450
00:50:47,485 --> 00:50:49,285
Where have you been, Aktemur Bey

451
00:50:49,385 --> 00:50:51,465
I've been looking for
you since morning.

452
00:50:52,015 --> 00:50:54,685
Why are you looking for me?

453
00:50:55,145 --> 00:50:56,515
Did you talk to her?

454
00:50:56,535 --> 00:50:57,915
Yes, I did.

455
00:50:58,905 --> 00:51:00,225
What does she say?

456
00:51:00,245 --> 00:51:01,685
Wait, let me catch my breath.

457
00:51:02,995 --> 00:51:04,675
My throat is dry.

458
00:51:05,075 --> 00:51:08,645
Should I drink something?

459
00:51:10,455 --> 00:51:12,625
Sherbet seller, give us sherbet.

460
00:51:19,995 --> 00:51:21,115
Thank you.

461
00:51:23,755 --> 00:51:25,045
Thank you.

462
00:51:25,975 --> 00:51:27,485
Tell me now.

463
00:51:34,305 --> 00:51:36,575
What did she say?
Is her heart empty?

464
00:51:39,435 --> 00:51:40,735
That will not happen.

465
00:51:41,845 --> 00:51:43,565
That girl is tough.

466
00:51:46,105 --> 00:51:47,485
Forget about her.

467
00:51:48,185 --> 00:51:50,255
I will find a better one for you.

468
00:52:01,895 --> 00:52:03,405
Thank Allah.

469
00:52:04,035 --> 00:52:06,175
Thank you, my Bey.

470
00:52:09,455 --> 00:52:11,485
You say it won't happen, right?

471
00:52:14,625 --> 00:52:16,455
Does she love someone?

472
00:52:25,725 --> 00:52:27,875
Good news!

473
00:52:28,515 --> 00:52:29,875
What will you buy me?

474
00:52:29,905 --> 00:52:31,395
Whatever you want, Ülgen Hatun.

475
00:52:31,405 --> 00:52:33,205
Come on, what did the girl say?

476
00:52:33,565 --> 00:52:35,135
Her heart is empty.

477
00:52:35,925 --> 00:52:37,725
However, she is a brave girl.

478
00:52:37,835 --> 00:52:39,575
She wants a brave man like her.

479
00:52:39,845 --> 00:52:41,035
And?

480
00:52:42,185 --> 00:52:44,355
Shewill not find someone braver than you.

481
00:52:44,445 --> 00:52:45,975
You're right.

482
00:52:56,235 --> 00:52:57,825
So, Bengi Hatun?

483
00:52:58,665 --> 00:53:01,005
They bring fabrics from
different countries.

484
00:53:01,955 --> 00:53:04,375
Fabrics that never seen in these areas.

485
00:53:04,665 --> 00:53:06,215
So beautiful, Marta.

486
00:53:06,275 --> 00:53:08,805
We should prepare Alçiçek's
dowry with you.

487
00:53:09,475 --> 00:53:13,575
Me and my cloths are at your command, Bengi Hatun.

488
00:53:15,035 --> 00:53:16,625
Bala Hatun.

489
00:53:17,725 --> 00:53:19,265
A raid took place near Karaağaç.

490
00:53:19,315 --> 00:53:21,355
Turks entered Makri village.

491
00:53:21,765 --> 00:53:23,085
Turks?

492
00:53:24,165 --> 00:53:25,475
Tell Turgut Bey quickly.

493
00:53:25,945 --> 00:53:27,995
Come on sisters.

494
00:53:29,135 --> 00:53:30,665
What do they say, Alçiçek?

495
00:53:31,245 --> 00:53:32,745
Batur, my brother.

496
00:53:33,715 --> 00:53:35,235
Tell Öktem Bey.

497
00:53:35,625 --> 00:53:36,675
How does this happen?

498
00:53:36,795 --> 00:53:39,335
My uncle Batur Alp works
to protect Christians.

499
00:53:39,465 --> 00:53:40,985
Peace is on.

500
00:53:41,035 --> 00:53:44,155
Which Turkmen disobeys the order
of Osman Bey and attacks Makri?

501
00:53:44,685 --> 00:53:47,735
Don't worry, there is clearly
something wrong with this.

502
00:53:48,435 --> 00:53:50,005
Alps!

503
00:53:51,125 --> 00:53:53,425
Let's go to the tribe quickly!

504
00:53:59,765 --> 00:54:02,005
I don't know who you are
and what you are.

505
00:54:03,755 --> 00:54:06,535
But if your hand is stained with
the blood of our Alps...

506
00:54:07,775 --> 00:54:09,505
there is no escape for you.

507
00:54:10,365 --> 00:54:14,915
Your men burned the village
and took the gold.

508
00:54:15,975 --> 00:54:17,565
And I took their souls.

509
00:54:18,365 --> 00:54:20,475
The price of blood is paid with blood.

510
00:54:23,005 --> 00:54:24,865
If I wasn't here for peace...

511
00:54:26,245 --> 00:54:27,635
I'd kill you.

512
00:54:28,165 --> 00:54:31,945
I will kill you and your dogs!

513
00:54:32,595 --> 00:54:34,185
You ignoble dog!

514
00:54:34,305 --> 00:54:36,175
Stop, Öktem Bey!

515
00:54:36,245 --> 00:54:37,785
Öktem Bey!

516
00:54:37,885 --> 00:54:39,935
I know your pain, Öktem Bey.

517
00:54:40,015 --> 00:54:41,655
I had many martyrs in my tribe.

518
00:54:41,765 --> 00:54:42,985
I lost many martyrs.

519
00:54:43,075 --> 00:54:44,655
Not now!

520
00:54:48,555 --> 00:54:50,585
You will leave now and go...

521
00:54:52,285 --> 00:54:53,825
but don't forget...

522
00:54:54,275 --> 00:54:58,865
You will account for the massacre you
carried out and the gold you took.

523
00:54:59,185 --> 00:55:00,755
Öktem Bey!

524
00:55:02,625 --> 00:55:04,215
Turgut Bey!

525
00:55:04,335 --> 00:55:05,915
Is this death appropriate?

526
00:55:05,985 --> 00:55:07,805
We will not leave our Alps here.

527
00:55:10,105 --> 00:55:12,395
It's a good thing I didn't kill you.

528
00:55:13,055 --> 00:55:14,845
The dead you ask for...

529
00:55:17,335 --> 00:55:20,675
Your bey Osman is the one who
will come and take them.

530
00:55:22,325 --> 00:55:23,675
Stop.

531
00:55:24,525 --> 00:55:25,905
Stop

532
00:55:26,435 --> 00:55:27,955
Not now.

533
00:55:32,085 --> 00:55:33,655
Not now.

534
00:55:44,350 --> 00:55:45,650
Olof.

535
00:56:00,160 --> 00:56:02,010
The moment I put my hand down...

536
00:56:02,400 --> 00:56:06,080
the breath you take will be the
last.

537
00:56:15,400 --> 00:56:17,420
We are good at fighting...

538
00:56:18,310 --> 00:56:20,690
and we also fight lies and slander.

539
00:56:22,180 --> 00:56:26,720
But we always know that the truth
will come out sooner or later.

540
00:56:26,760 --> 00:56:30,950
If I find out that you are behind this, I
will rip your liver out with my own hands.

541
00:56:36,710 --> 00:56:38,940
But now, I'm here to make peace.

542
00:56:42,190 --> 00:56:43,720
Don't worry.

543
00:56:44,650 --> 00:56:46,050
Our leader is one.

544
00:56:48,540 --> 00:56:50,750
Osman bey will come and take our martyrs.

545
00:56:51,910 --> 00:56:53,130
Until then...

546
00:56:55,130 --> 00:56:56,750
your breath is counted.

547
00:57:01,490 --> 00:57:02,750
Know its worth.

548
00:57:09,930 --> 00:57:11,800
Trust me Öktem Bey.

549
00:57:12,950 --> 00:57:14,700
Go back to your tent.

550
00:57:36,270 --> 00:57:38,060
Let's go, Alps!

551
00:57:40,230 --> 00:57:41,570
Come on.

552
00:57:49,760 --> 00:57:52,120
Constantinople, Emperor's Palace

553
00:57:52,585 --> 00:57:55,645
In order to claim Byzantium throne...

554
00:57:56,675 --> 00:57:59,345
one must have the blood of the
dynasty.

555
00:58:01,295 --> 00:58:04,275
My commanders, my advisors...

556
00:58:05,365 --> 00:58:07,775
The Crown Princes with
whom I am linked by blood.

557
00:58:10,585 --> 00:58:12,555
I don't know where the enemy is.

558
00:58:15,295 --> 00:58:16,955
Maybe in my nearest place.

559
00:58:18,435 --> 00:58:23,375
If you only look at the places near you, you
will not be able to see the big picture, Emperor.

560
00:58:25,025 --> 00:58:30,555
That is, I will change my point of view
if I can not change events.

561
00:58:30,655 --> 00:58:31,845
Right?

562
00:58:31,895 --> 00:58:38,255
If you let me, I'd like to question the
keeper Sarkis and all who were there.

563
00:58:38,495 --> 00:58:40,455
Don't worry, Kantakuzenos.

564
00:58:40,785 --> 00:58:42,925
My daughter Ophelia is in the ring now.

565
00:58:44,335 --> 00:58:45,905
Ophelia.

566
00:58:53,845 --> 00:58:58,185
Water the ring with your sweat, lest it is
watered with your blood.

567
00:58:58,755 --> 00:59:00,035
Raise your shield.

568
00:59:08,425 --> 00:59:09,675
Yes.

569
00:59:20,595 --> 00:59:21,905
My Bey.

570
00:59:21,975 --> 00:59:23,745
Have we been exposed?

571
00:59:39,205 --> 00:59:40,905
Are you their leader?

572
00:59:43,225 --> 00:59:44,775
I am Sarkis.

573
00:59:45,675 --> 00:59:46,995
The arena keeper.

574
00:59:50,835 --> 00:59:52,885
I am the most loyal servant of
your dynasty.

575
00:59:55,165 --> 00:59:58,165
Then, you also fought for
my father on that bloody day.

576
00:59:59,525 --> 01:00:00,725
Yes, Princess Ophelia.

577
01:00:01,895 --> 01:00:06,765
The lives of us mortals are of no value to
the soul of a great emperor.

578
01:00:10,535 --> 01:00:12,195
We fought against traitors.

579
01:00:13,905 --> 01:00:17,315
An act so noble that we do not expect
from slaves

580
01:00:20,775 --> 01:00:23,145
Well, aren't you in
charge of this arena?

581
01:00:26,305 --> 01:00:27,375
Yes, I am.

582
01:00:27,445 --> 01:00:30,525
Where were you when those
traitors slipped into the arena?

583
01:00:31,985 --> 01:00:34,725
Where were you when they
came through the doors?

584
01:00:35,965 --> 01:00:38,935
Where were you when the
Emperor's life was being targeted?

585
01:00:40,465 --> 01:00:42,045
Princess Ophelia, we...-

586
01:00:48,635 --> 01:00:50,645
Your moves were spoiled
when the Turks came.

587
01:00:51,655 --> 01:00:53,795
You changed your side, too.

588
01:00:54,775 --> 01:00:58,435
No slave would give up on hi life
for the sake of a noble.

589
01:00:58,525 --> 01:01:00,115
Catch him.

590
01:01:04,445 --> 01:01:06,525
As Princess Ophelia would like...

591
01:01:17,485 --> 01:01:18,715
Great Emperor

592
01:01:18,755 --> 01:01:22,535
A unit of Osman Bey attacked the town of
Makri, near Marmaracık.

593
01:01:22,795 --> 01:01:24,665
They killed the Christians.

594
01:01:25,565 --> 01:01:28,315
This... is not possible.

595
01:01:28,725 --> 01:01:31,285
We left our brothers to them!

596
01:01:32,085 --> 01:01:34,675
We shouldn't have trusted
Osman from the beginning.

597
01:01:36,185 --> 01:01:39,675
We have a peace agreement, he can't
be the one who did this.

598
01:01:39,725 --> 01:01:41,545
The taxes were distributed in Makri.

599
01:01:41,965 --> 01:01:43,825
So, gold has blinded Osman's eye.

600
01:01:43,965 --> 01:01:45,915
This should not be left unaccounted for.

601
01:01:45,955 --> 01:01:47,955
Gold, Kantakuzenos?

602
01:01:48,255 --> 01:01:50,085
I gave him more than that.

603
01:01:52,945 --> 01:01:54,725
Osman isn't the one to do this.

604
01:01:59,145 --> 01:02:00,525
I will learn what happened

605
01:02:01,675 --> 01:02:04,525
If you'll excuse me, I can
find out what's inside.

606
01:02:10,705 --> 01:02:12,495
You will go as my representative.

607
01:02:13,015 --> 01:02:16,095
You will learn what happened and tell me.

608
01:02:16,715 --> 01:02:17,975
Immediately.

609
01:02:18,385 --> 01:02:21,235
And I'll never come back
here before I learn.

610
01:02:21,615 --> 01:02:22,865
Excuse me.

611
01:02:26,585 --> 01:02:29,325
I have work to do here before then.

612
01:02:29,905 --> 01:02:31,925
Karacahisar Castle

613
01:02:38,885 --> 01:02:40,625
Hold your breath, son.

614
01:02:41,015 --> 01:02:42,515
No...

615
01:02:45,545 --> 01:02:47,705
but he will hold the reins
of his management.

616
01:02:53,725 --> 01:02:56,245
Orhan, get on your feet.

617
01:03:10,305 --> 01:03:11,815
You fell into the trap.

618
01:03:14,765 --> 01:03:16,535
You fell into the hands of the enemy.

619
01:03:19,475 --> 01:03:21,825
You make your mother bandage
your wounds too!

620
01:03:31,215 --> 01:03:32,605
Orhan

621
01:03:36,735 --> 01:03:38,745
who does not bandage his own wound...

622
01:03:41,705 --> 01:03:43,475
can't heal.

623
01:03:46,635 --> 01:03:48,635
You will do your own thing.

624
01:03:49,895 --> 01:03:51,435
You will...

625
01:03:56,545 --> 01:03:58,365
so that you will have strength.

626
01:04:03,995 --> 01:04:06,015
Put your finger back in place now.

627
01:04:09,365 --> 01:04:11,395
You made me the Bey of Karacahisar.

628
01:04:20,155 --> 01:04:21,925
- Son.
- I don't want it, mother.

629
01:04:52,735 --> 01:04:54,255
Leave it, mother.

630
01:05:17,655 --> 01:05:20,165
I do what I can do
to be fit for my position.

631
01:05:23,645 --> 01:05:25,655
Trust your son, Osman Bey.

632
01:05:32,725 --> 01:05:36,735
I used to see you small and hold you to my
chest because you are my son...

633
01:05:37,905 --> 01:05:41,515
You became a strong Bey.

634
01:05:42,065 --> 01:05:43,815
I didn't notice that.

635
01:05:52,145 --> 01:05:54,695
My goal is to be a
son worthy of Osman Bey.

636
01:05:54,875 --> 01:05:57,035
Who is Osman Bey to accept you?

637
01:06:05,535 --> 01:06:06,855
What is important is...

638
01:06:09,065 --> 01:06:10,845
to be acceptable to Allah.

639
01:06:14,125 --> 01:06:15,465
What is important...

640
01:06:17,625 --> 01:06:20,225
is to be worthy of Allah.

641
01:06:28,795 --> 01:06:30,855
Öktem Tent

642
01:06:31,485 --> 01:06:32,955
I feel bored, Alçiçek.

643
01:06:33,105 --> 01:06:35,605
No news yet. I can't stand here.

644
01:06:42,135 --> 01:06:43,445
Öktem.

645
01:06:43,615 --> 01:06:45,405
My Bey, welcome.

646
01:06:45,715 --> 01:06:47,515
Where is Batur?
Is he outside?

647
01:06:47,715 --> 01:06:48,605
Hatun...

648
01:06:48,745 --> 01:06:51,585
Why aren't you telling us anything?

649
01:06:51,665 --> 01:06:52,385
Hatun.

650
01:06:52,395 --> 01:06:56,065
He must be hungry now. Is it easy to
raise the sword against the infidels?

651
01:06:56,095 --> 01:06:57,255
Let me summon him.

652
01:06:57,405 --> 01:06:58,985
Hatun.

653
01:07:01,945 --> 01:07:04,495
Batur is not here.
He will not come.

654
01:07:09,585 --> 01:07:10,855
No.

655
01:07:12,605 --> 01:07:14,655
I see you only speak evil.

656
01:07:15,175 --> 01:07:17,675
- Hatun.
- Don't tell me that!

657
01:07:20,845 --> 01:07:26,265
Batur fell a martyr.

658
01:07:34,165 --> 01:07:35,895
We couldn't take his body.

659
01:07:46,555 --> 01:07:48,255
But we will take him.

660
01:07:51,585 --> 01:07:52,965
We'll take him.

661
01:08:02,215 --> 01:08:07,435
Where is my brother, Oktem Bey?

662
01:08:08,025 --> 01:08:09,345
I will bring him.

663
01:08:09,385 --> 01:08:12,755
You brought him neither alive nor dead!

664
01:08:12,845 --> 01:08:14,135
Hatun, I'll bring him.

665
01:08:14,135 --> 01:08:15,215
Couldn't you take him?

666
01:08:15,255 --> 01:08:16,995
I'll bring him, Hatun!
Stay patient!

667
01:08:17,045 --> 01:08:18,785
- Couldn't you take him?
- Hatun!

668
01:08:18,785 --> 01:08:19,635
Couldn't you take him?

669
01:08:19,635 --> 01:08:20,604
I will bring him!

670
01:08:20,604 --> 01:08:22,604
Did you leave him to those ignoble dogs!?

671
01:08:34,705 --> 01:08:38,564
Why do you carry this sword?

672
01:08:57,845 --> 01:08:59,585
May I, my Bey?

673
01:09:00,404 --> 01:09:01,984
Come in, Huseyin.

674
01:09:13,814 --> 01:09:15,345
You can get out.

675
01:09:26,635 --> 01:09:29,305
Yes, tell me, let's see, Huseyin.

676
01:09:31,035 --> 01:09:33,035
Talk about what you saw and heard.

677
01:09:33,154 --> 01:09:36,845
Suddenly infidels raided, my Bey.
They were disguised as alps.

678
01:09:38,365 --> 01:09:41,475
They killed the people
in the village first.

679
01:09:42,115 --> 01:09:44,875
And then the Alps of Oktem Bey.

680
01:09:47,715 --> 01:09:49,385
Who did this?
Did you see them?

681
01:09:49,725 --> 01:09:52,075
Olof, his name is Olof, my Bey.

682
01:09:55,575 --> 01:09:57,155
Olof ha?

683
01:09:58,875 --> 01:10:00,215
Olof.

684
01:10:05,625 --> 01:10:11,675
Don't tell anyone until we understand
their purpose in this attack.

685
01:10:12,735 --> 01:10:14,795
Keep tracking those dogs.

686
01:10:15,305 --> 01:10:18,335
I'll track them, my Bey.

687
01:10:19,045 --> 01:10:21,325
Are we not going to tell
anyone about this?

688
01:10:21,585 --> 01:10:23,115
Stop there, Huseyin.

689
01:10:24,395 --> 01:10:26,485
Let Osman Bey weaken.

690
01:10:27,415 --> 01:10:33,205
Let him weaken so that we gain
power more easily.

691
01:10:36,275 --> 01:10:41,495
We will say what we know
when the right time comes.

692
01:10:42,415 --> 01:10:45,225
But not now.

693
01:10:53,775 --> 01:10:55,515
Macri Area

694
01:10:56,285 --> 01:10:59,095
Osman did not reach his goal, my love.

695
01:11:00,445 --> 01:11:05,155
The messengers he sent to the emperor
exist no longer.

696
01:11:05,375 --> 01:11:12,315
They must have thought how beautiful
the angel of death is...

697
01:11:12,315 --> 01:11:14,865
...while you kill them.

698
01:11:15,355 --> 01:11:17,905
I don't think
they could think of anything.

699
01:11:18,145 --> 01:11:23,585
Osman will experience the pain of
losing a child.

700
01:11:25,085 --> 01:11:28,205
I'll take Orhan from him.

701
01:11:28,555 --> 01:11:33,585
He'll pay for every drop of Saga's blood.

702
01:11:37,015 --> 01:11:40,725
He will sent this as an evidence
to the emperor.

703
01:11:41,725 --> 01:11:44,305
It's Saga's.

704
01:11:49,155 --> 01:11:51,415
Saga.

705
01:12:04,495 --> 01:12:06,045
Osman!

706
01:12:06,475 --> 01:12:09,605
He came just as we were about to
kill Orhan.

707
01:12:09,875 --> 01:12:13,595
We lost all our men.

708
01:12:15,975 --> 01:12:19,885
Dan, Dan, where is he?!

709
01:12:20,075 --> 01:12:22,195
He was captured by Osman.

710
01:12:22,885 --> 01:12:27,655
So he was captured by Osman!

711
01:12:28,325 --> 01:12:33,225
So he was captured by Osman!

712
01:12:35,935 --> 01:12:37,425
Frig!

713
01:12:37,595 --> 01:12:41,445
Go to Yenişehir right now and wait
for my word.

714
01:12:42,305 --> 01:12:44,585
We will hurt Osman.

715
01:12:54,835 --> 01:12:57,545
Tell me what's going on in Karacahisar.

716
01:12:57,885 --> 01:12:59,975
I had provisions counted.

717
01:13:00,245 --> 01:13:01,595
Our warehouses are full.

718
01:13:01,875 --> 01:13:05,145
Merchants come from all over the world
Our market is growing, my Bey.

719
01:13:05,845 --> 01:13:09,435
I also detected the poor.
The aid will reach them soon.

720
01:13:11,735 --> 01:13:14,545
I always do the job I've seen
from my elders, my Bey.

721
01:13:17,575 --> 01:13:19,395
Let's eat then.

722
01:13:21,085 --> 01:13:23,815
In the name of Allah
the merciful, the compassionate

723
01:13:23,915 --> 01:13:26,355
In the name of Allah
the merciful, the compassionate

724
01:13:28,665 --> 01:13:30,775
Enjoy your meal.

725
01:13:55,845 --> 01:13:59,295
Ask me the question that
stops you from eating.

726
01:14:05,005 --> 01:14:07,655
Who are the ones who attacked me, Dad?

727
01:14:10,625 --> 01:14:15,815
We came to this world for a test, son

728
01:14:16,485 --> 01:14:19,245
We came to fight the devil

729
01:14:20,475 --> 01:14:24,525
But most people do not know about this.

730
01:14:25,835 --> 01:14:31,375
These demons are the ones who attacked you.

731
01:14:32,635 --> 01:14:35,285
We don't know how they attack,
when they attack.

732
01:14:35,635 --> 01:14:38,745
But this does not prevent us
from defeating them

733
01:14:40,595 --> 01:14:47,315
Because there is no victory
for the devil against Allah's people.

734
01:14:53,365 --> 01:14:54,915
Orhan!

735
01:14:56,255 --> 01:15:02,635
Under this earth is full of these demons.

736
01:15:06,085 --> 01:15:07,935
We are growing bigger.

737
01:15:08,365 --> 01:15:13,045
The greater we are, the more enemy
we will have.

738
01:15:13,205 --> 01:15:15,295
But we will trample them all, Inshallah.

739
01:15:15,455 --> 01:15:17,925
Our problems get bigger,
but we get bigger as well.

740
01:15:18,435 --> 01:15:20,685
We will fight, Inshallah, mother!

741
01:15:20,815 --> 01:15:22,445
Mashallah! (praise be!)

742
01:15:22,765 --> 01:15:26,495
You have the power to fight.

743
01:15:26,865 --> 01:15:29,035
Yes we have.

744
01:15:29,035 --> 01:15:31,035
We have.

745
01:15:33,345 --> 01:15:36,615
Come on, Orhan.

746
01:15:37,175 --> 01:15:44,385
Eat your food and comfort your father
when the time comes.

747
01:15:46,445 --> 01:15:47,625
Come on.

748
01:16:00,745 --> 01:16:05,185
Do you know why Osman went
to Constantinople?

749
01:16:05,615 --> 01:16:08,325
Our worries are out of our heads,
Bayindir Bey!

750
01:16:08,595 --> 01:16:09,925
What are you talking about?

751
01:16:10,095 --> 01:16:13,835
I'm talking about who caused these
worries, Bengi Hatun.

752
01:16:20,535 --> 01:16:22,895
They attacked the emperor.

753
01:16:23,695 --> 01:16:27,095
Our Osman Bey went to save him.

754
01:16:27,225 --> 01:16:34,115
He obviously stepped on someone's tail
while protecting him.

755
01:16:34,275 --> 01:16:38,985
You want to say that these dogs
came to hurt us.

756
01:16:40,965 --> 01:16:44,185
If they really didn't do
anything in that village

757
01:16:45,525 --> 01:16:48,495
This means that our men died
for nothing.

758
01:16:50,175 --> 01:16:56,095
There are no deads, Bayindir Bey.
There are martyrs.

759
01:16:56,555 --> 01:16:58,265
Eyvallah. (Right)

760
01:17:15,055 --> 01:17:16,665
Thank you.

761
01:17:28,205 --> 01:17:29,225
Mother...

762
01:17:29,355 --> 01:17:31,345
You haven't eaten anything.

763
01:17:31,555 --> 01:17:33,025
At least drink this.

764
01:17:33,105 --> 01:17:38,675
I won't take a bite until
my brother's body arrives.

765
01:17:44,755 --> 01:17:47,385
We shouldn't have left the valiants there.

766
01:17:47,595 --> 01:17:50,245
If it wasn't for Turgut Bey...

767
01:17:50,435 --> 01:17:53,035
They are just trying to stop us.

768
01:17:54,635 --> 01:17:57,535
If it was not for Osman...

769
01:17:57,905 --> 01:18:00,295
...We wouldn't be broken.

770
01:18:02,675 --> 01:18:05,515
If it wasn't for Turgut...

771
01:18:06,235 --> 01:18:09,665
We wouldn't leave our martyrs there.

772
01:18:10,175 --> 01:18:15,745
Does that Turgut call himself a Bey
after he left our martyrs to infidels?

773
01:18:19,085 --> 01:18:22,655
I want my brother, Oktem Bey.

774
01:18:23,665 --> 01:18:28,705
You will find me in my brother's
empty grave until he comes

775
01:18:31,515 --> 01:18:41,525
Tomorrow morning
I will bring our martyrs and avenge us.

776
01:18:48,115 --> 01:18:50,665
The axe of whom set up the trap that day.

777
01:18:56,605 --> 01:18:59,075
The signs are the same.

778
01:19:02,335 --> 01:19:06,085
You say the ones who attacked us and
the ones who attacked Orhan are the same.

779
01:19:07,985 --> 01:19:12,835
We see them whenever
we are in a trap.

780
01:19:13,075 --> 01:19:18,135
This means that they are the ones who attacked
the village and killed the innocents.

781
01:19:18,355 --> 01:19:23,285
Batur and his followers followed this too
and wanted to stop them when they saw it.

782
01:19:24,515 --> 01:19:26,465
But they killed our martyrs.

783
01:19:26,685 --> 01:19:30,435
These snakes blamed them
after they killed them!

784
01:19:30,565 --> 01:19:33,085
They started after
we protected the emperor

785
01:19:34,365 --> 01:19:36,955
Apparently, they are trying to
drag us into the war.

786
01:19:37,105 --> 01:19:39,945
They want to drag us into the war

787
01:19:39,945 --> 01:19:42,935
In order to weaken us and the emperor.

788
01:19:45,215 --> 01:19:53,195
There is someone they hide in the dark secretly
in these attacks, Osman Bey.

789
01:19:53,995 --> 01:19:56,785
They are waiting for me to
deliver the martyrs.

790
01:19:57,535 --> 01:19:59,805
Now that they have a game...

791
01:20:00,025 --> 01:20:03,395
Let's say game on.

792
01:20:04,305 --> 01:20:06,615
We will be careful.

793
01:20:06,855 --> 01:20:09,185
When I face them...

794
01:20:10,945 --> 01:20:12,985
You will take martyrs.

795
01:20:13,145 --> 01:20:17,885
We will not forget the martyrs of course,
and the treachery surrounding them

796
01:20:18,075 --> 01:20:20,485
We have to hurry now.

797
01:20:20,755 --> 01:20:23,085
Oktem may do something crazy
before we arrive.

798
01:20:23,345 --> 01:20:25,275
The fire of revenge ignites his heart.

799
01:20:25,415 --> 01:20:28,085
Their intention is clear.

800
01:20:29,375 --> 01:20:31,895
We are on a thin rope.

801
01:20:33,825 --> 01:20:35,985
If it breaks...

802
01:20:37,325 --> 01:20:41,345
Then we will find ourselves
broken on the battlefield

803
01:20:42,875 --> 01:20:45,415
But we will not allow this.

804
01:20:45,635 --> 01:20:48,575
We'll find the person behind them first.

805
01:20:49,215 --> 01:20:50,755
Oktem.

806
01:20:51,735 --> 01:20:54,525
He will stay behind
the curtain of secrecy

807
01:20:56,125 --> 01:21:01,105
We'll raise that curtain
and dig their roots!

808
01:21:02,235 --> 01:21:07,315
It's tme to start things now.

809
01:21:24,475 --> 01:21:26,835
This is my brother Boran.

810
01:21:34,985 --> 01:21:38,255
And I am Cerkutay.

811
01:21:45,740 --> 01:21:47,770
I am not a sword, gentlemen.

812
01:21:49,130 --> 01:21:51,100
You can't make me good
by beating me!

813
01:21:51,740 --> 01:21:54,270
I am the great wave
that will bring you down!

814
01:22:00,780 --> 01:22:04,230
But all these wounds are open
he will smell!

815
01:22:06,650 --> 01:22:08,800
Masha Allah (praise be)

816
01:22:12,940 --> 01:22:17,230
We'll salt you now
so you don't smell like that

817
01:22:22,010 --> 01:22:25,040
Open, open, open, open!

818
01:22:39,880 --> 01:22:41,900
You idiots!

819
01:22:43,320 --> 01:22:47,190
Do you think you can scare a man who
defeated seas to come here with salt?

820
01:22:49,550 --> 01:22:57,920
I will whip your head
and cover it with camel skin

821
01:23:03,200 --> 01:23:06,910
Stop, stop, stop!

822
01:23:10,790 --> 01:23:12,160
I will talk.

823
01:23:12,350 --> 01:23:14,580
Constantinople.

824
01:23:20,585 --> 01:23:22,645
You opened the gates for them.

825
01:23:23,365 --> 01:23:25,145
Come on, confess!

826
01:23:25,835 --> 01:23:27,835
Confess that we kill you quickly!

827
01:23:28,245 --> 01:23:30,345
We and the Turks saved the emperor.

828
01:23:30,585 --> 01:23:33,955
Turk's are gone.
We are here.

829
01:23:34,605 --> 01:23:39,405
And you, princess, would like to kill
us who prevented the attack.

830
01:23:41,565 --> 01:23:44,275
You're the one who wanted
to kill the emperor, right?

831
01:23:47,455 --> 01:23:51,985
Are you accusing me of
trying to kill my father?

832
01:23:52,265 --> 01:23:55,515
So it was you who would sit on the throne
after the emperor died?

833
01:23:55,995 --> 01:23:57,575
But you failed!

834
01:24:00,095 --> 01:24:02,595
You will pay the price
for this disrespect!

835
01:24:03,585 --> 01:24:05,115
Soldiers!

836
01:24:13,915 --> 01:24:15,495
Princess Ophelia!

837
01:24:15,935 --> 01:24:18,125
I always have a secret weapon and secrets.

838
01:24:20,805 --> 01:24:23,215
But I am not going to
be disrespectful for you.

839
01:24:24,655 --> 01:24:26,645
My body and soul is
under your command.

840
01:24:32,985 --> 01:24:34,495
You are not the guilty.

841
01:24:35,665 --> 01:24:37,355
You are clearly on my side.

842
01:24:39,545 --> 01:24:41,105
But... stop

843
01:24:44,375 --> 01:24:45,905
Stand up

844
01:24:51,035 --> 01:24:53,315
But I am not a person
whou would kill her father.

845
01:24:54,305 --> 01:24:56,815
I am always at your command,
Princess Ophelia.

846
01:24:57,105 --> 01:24:58,605
Well, who was this?

847
01:24:59,785 --> 01:25:01,285
Princess Ophelia.

848
01:25:11,925 --> 01:25:13,485
Princess Ophelia.

849
01:25:15,245 --> 01:25:16,995
What is happening here?

850
01:25:17,065 --> 01:25:19,255
The interrogation continues,
Kantakuzenos.

851
01:25:19,495 --> 01:25:21,195
We are looking for the traitors.

852
01:25:23,845 --> 01:25:25,715
Well, what did he tell you?

853
01:25:26,645 --> 01:25:29,465
He told that the emperor
was aimed to kill.

854
01:25:31,535 --> 01:25:33,785
But he doesn't know who did this.

855
01:25:38,825 --> 01:25:42,435
Did he also tell how he got those
traitors into the arena?

856
01:25:43,855 --> 01:25:46,945
Did he tell what he did while Sen Tahor
deploy his men?

857
01:25:50,895 --> 01:25:52,455
He didn't.

858
01:25:54,645 --> 01:25:57,025
The ring was under his responsibility

859
01:25:57,225 --> 01:25:59,335
The things that happened
is his fault.

860
01:26:01,145 --> 01:26:04,435
Prince Kantakuzenos,
leave him now!

861
01:26:11,615 --> 01:26:14,075
There is nothing else
we can learn from these.

862
01:26:15,785 --> 01:26:19,205
But obviously there are
others that we need to question!

863
01:26:19,955 --> 01:26:21,875
This business is filthy and bloody.

864
01:26:22,995 --> 01:26:24,505
Don't you worry.

865
01:26:24,875 --> 01:26:26,975
I will catch them all and punish them.

866
01:26:27,715 --> 01:26:29,775
Go to the palace, please.

867
01:26:37,915 --> 01:26:40,535
I'll be back for you again Sarkes.
Don't forget that.

868
01:26:40,655 --> 01:26:43,205
Our arena is always open to
Kantakuzenos.

869
01:26:57,595 --> 01:26:59,645
I don't see a
good expression on your face

870
01:27:00,165 --> 01:27:02,705
You obviously came
with bad news, what happened?

871
01:27:02,705 --> 01:27:04,705
Oh, Prince Kantakuzenos.

872
01:27:06,345 --> 01:27:07,935
Orhan is alive.

873
01:27:10,245 --> 01:27:12,655
And Dan is captivated by Osman.

874
01:27:14,975 --> 01:27:16,875
The cloud of mist is rising.

875
01:27:17,495 --> 01:27:20,975
I thought of all possibilities I
win in every possibility

876
01:27:22,035 --> 01:27:26,165
I will set off tomorrow.
Let's reveal the unknown.

877
01:27:26,165 --> 01:27:28,955
Have your eyes on Ophelia and Sarkes.

878
01:27:54,585 --> 01:27:56,625
Oktem's Tribe

879
01:28:00,085 --> 01:28:01,425
Alps!

880
01:28:04,655 --> 01:28:06,695
Blood for blood!

881
01:28:07,685 --> 01:28:10,985
To avenge the martyrs, come on!

882
01:28:18,805 --> 01:28:22,865
The great lord of the karken tribe,
Oktem Bey. Go and see

883
01:28:23,415 --> 01:28:26,735
But there is a saying "who starts up in
anger sits down with a loss"

884
01:28:26,825 --> 01:28:28,535
- Huseyin!
- Yes my Bey.

885
01:28:28,695 --> 01:28:30,205
Prepare your alps.

886
01:28:31,205 --> 01:28:33,545
We can't leave Oktem Bey alone.

887
01:28:53,465 --> 01:28:54,755
What's it, Oktem Bey?

888
01:29:00,925 --> 01:29:03,125
Join us if you want to help us.

889
01:29:03,845 --> 01:29:09,555
But if you're here to stop us,
don't try, Boran.

890
01:29:20,065 --> 01:29:21,775
It is the order of Osman Bey.

891
01:29:22,995 --> 01:29:27,055
No one will go out of their tribe.
No one will draw their weapon.

892
01:29:27,755 --> 01:29:29,095
Boran!

893
01:29:30,445 --> 01:29:33,965
Will you make me shed a brother's blood
instead of avenging the martyr's blood?

894
01:29:34,335 --> 01:29:35,885
The order is clear.

895
01:29:36,145 --> 01:29:39,145
No one with a sword will
go out of their tribe!

896
01:29:40,595 --> 01:29:45,445
If you don't stop, we might have to draw
our swords and shed blood, Oktem Bey.

897
01:29:48,485 --> 01:29:50,575
It's not my fault now.

898
01:30:00,225 --> 01:30:01,585
Stop!

899
01:30:02,975 --> 01:30:04,525
Oktem Bey!

900
01:30:06,095 --> 01:30:07,675
Boran Alp!

901
01:30:17,635 --> 01:30:18,955
My sheik.

902
01:30:24,565 --> 01:30:27,445
You let discord
walk around you, Oktem Bey.

903
01:30:27,445 --> 01:30:33,625
My Sheik, don't.
Open my way.

904
01:30:36,255 --> 01:30:38,765
Evil seems to be present
in your way.

905
01:30:39,785 --> 01:30:43,555
So let me abide by the words
of the Messenger of Allah, who said:

906
01:30:43,555 --> 01:30:46,505
"The sitting is better
than the one standing...

907
01:30:46,505 --> 01:30:50,895
and the one standing is better than
the one walking when there is discord"

908
01:30:53,135 --> 01:30:56,315
Sit down, Oktem Bey.
Sit down.

909
01:30:58,795 --> 01:30:59,875
My sheik is right!

910
01:31:02,885 --> 01:31:05,035
- Welcome my sheik!
- Eyvallah (thank you)

911
01:31:06,085 --> 01:31:09,555
Falling out with each other
is what the enemy wants!

912
01:31:10,215 --> 01:31:11,555
Calm down.

913
01:31:13,715 --> 01:31:19,085
If Osman Bey told not to leave the tribe,
he must know something.

914
01:31:31,135 --> 01:31:33,135
Yeni Sehir.

915
01:31:46,650 --> 01:31:48,740
My condolences, Alcicek Hatun.

916
01:31:48,800 --> 01:31:50,380
May Allah grant you patience.

917
01:31:50,450 --> 01:31:53,400
Patience hah? Patience!?

918
01:31:54,540 --> 01:31:57,330
My uncle went there by order
of Osman Bey

919
01:31:57,960 --> 01:32:00,340
You are the reason
for what we lived!

920
01:32:00,930 --> 01:32:02,970
How do you keep telling me to
stay patient?

921
01:32:41,740 --> 01:32:43,570
Who are these, Subasi?

922
01:32:43,940 --> 01:32:45,640
We got news this morning.

923
01:32:47,070 --> 01:32:50,820
Osman Bey caught them when they
were about to attack Orhan Bey.

924
01:32:54,470 --> 01:32:56,210
They raided the village first.

925
01:32:57,790 --> 01:32:59,490
And they trapped Orhan.

926
01:33:00,320 --> 01:33:02,730
It is clear that
they are attacking from all fronts

927
01:33:03,280 --> 01:33:06,460
So you're telling me these are the ones
who killed my brother?

928
01:33:15,450 --> 01:33:17,480
Ignobles!

929
01:33:18,510 --> 01:33:20,040
Stop this Alcicek!

930
01:33:20,090 --> 01:33:22,140
I will not let my uncle down!

931
01:33:22,180 --> 01:33:23,540
Stop!

932
01:33:26,440 --> 01:33:27,830
Bengi Hatun!

933
01:33:27,860 --> 01:33:29,190
Bengi Hatun!

934
01:33:34,570 --> 01:33:35,900
Stop!

935
01:33:35,920 --> 01:33:37,990
Get out of my way, Bala Hatun!

936
01:33:39,240 --> 01:33:41,030
They killed our alps!

937
01:33:41,550 --> 01:33:43,260
They took my brother from me!

938
01:33:43,300 --> 01:33:44,680
Calm down!

939
01:33:44,820 --> 01:33:46,180
Get away.

940
01:33:48,370 --> 01:33:49,710
Alps!

941
01:33:49,710 --> 01:33:51,250
Put your swords down!

942
01:33:51,320 --> 01:33:52,900
Give me that dog!

943
01:33:53,760 --> 01:33:55,750
The blood of alps
is on their hands!

944
01:33:55,820 --> 01:33:57,130
Kill them!

945
01:33:57,870 --> 01:33:59,720
They didn't even give us our martyrs!

946
01:33:59,800 --> 01:34:02,880
Kill them!

947
01:34:03,750 --> 01:34:05,800
How do you let this happen?

948
01:34:15,030 --> 01:34:18,230
Let's say what we are doing is wrong.
Is what you are doing right?

949
01:34:18,560 --> 01:34:20,840
How can you draw your sword
to a captive?

950
01:34:25,570 --> 01:34:29,440
These dogs tried to kill my son.

951
01:34:29,880 --> 01:34:33,080
While I allow them to survive
in order to find out the truth...

952
01:34:33,080 --> 01:34:35,500
...what are you trying to achieve here,
Bengi Hatun?

953
01:34:35,560 --> 01:34:37,320
You should have killed them there!

954
01:34:38,130 --> 01:34:40,070
You shall not show mercy to the cruels!

955
01:34:40,070 --> 01:34:41,790
We don't have mercy on anyone!

956
01:34:43,080 --> 01:34:46,400
We bury our pain in our
hearts for the truth

957
01:34:46,510 --> 01:34:47,910
Be a little patient, Bengi Hatun!

958
01:34:48,690 --> 01:34:50,460
We all strive for the truth.

959
01:34:50,540 --> 01:34:52,560
How long will I be patient, Bala Hatun?

960
01:34:53,570 --> 01:34:56,020
My brother's grave is empty!!

961
01:35:00,610 --> 01:35:02,670
We have an unfinished business now.

962
01:35:05,950 --> 01:35:07,530
Alps!

963
01:35:12,630 --> 01:35:14,490
Bring the horses, come on!

964
01:35:16,700 --> 01:35:18,240
Alps!

965
01:35:18,840 --> 01:35:20,430
To the dungeon!

966
01:35:31,620 --> 01:35:33,140
Alcicek.

967
01:35:33,590 --> 01:35:36,880
Kill that dog at any cost.
Do it somehow.

968
01:35:40,550 --> 01:35:42,740
Move! Move!

969
01:35:43,610 --> 01:35:44,990
Hurry!

970
01:35:56,260 --> 01:35:59,760
I won't leave you in their hands, Dan.

971
01:36:04,785 --> 01:36:07,255
Marta, I brought you fresh fish.

972
01:36:36,805 --> 01:36:38,805
It's time to move, Leo.

973
01:36:40,265 --> 01:36:41,835
That Aladdin.

974
01:36:42,375 --> 01:36:43,655
Let's find out...

975
01:36:45,045 --> 01:36:46,585
...where he is.

976
01:36:55,165 --> 01:36:57,385
I bear witness
that there is no god but Allah...

977
01:36:57,415 --> 01:36:59,845
And I bear witness that Muhammad
is his Messenger.

978
01:37:19,485 --> 01:37:21,495
The strength we got...

979
01:37:22,045 --> 01:37:26,135
...has become famous all over the three
continents for years!

980
01:37:29,745 --> 01:37:32,365
Who came from the cold northern waters...

981
01:37:33,045 --> 01:37:37,625
...and turned The Mediterranean
into a lake of blood?

982
01:37:37,685 --> 01:37:40,965
We, sons of north!

983
01:37:41,715 --> 01:37:50,235
Who carries the cold north wind
and the fresh south breeze?

984
01:37:50,315 --> 01:37:53,235
We, sons of north!

985
01:37:56,335 --> 01:37:58,575
Vikings were our ancestors.

986
01:37:58,995 --> 01:38:02,415
We have been giving our blood for Rome
for a thousand years.

987
01:38:02,985 --> 01:38:04,585
We sacrificed our lives!

988
01:38:06,945 --> 01:38:08,815
What did we get in return?

989
01:38:11,785 --> 01:38:13,975
Their religion.

990
01:38:16,705 --> 01:38:19,695
We worshipped their Gods!

991
01:38:22,885 --> 01:38:27,505
While Rome was rotting
with fancy outfits and sweet smells...

992
01:38:28,605 --> 01:38:32,805
We turned the Mediterranean
into a bloodshed!

993
01:38:34,565 --> 01:38:42,095
But Rome couldn't take our souls!

994
01:38:46,645 --> 01:38:48,185
Right now...

995
01:38:48,885 --> 01:38:52,455
...It's time to take back what we have
been giving for a thousand years

996
01:39:06,285 --> 01:39:10,705
We blew the wind of north
in Jerusalem.

997
01:39:12,985 --> 01:39:15,295
Sometimes in Libya.

998
01:39:15,350 --> 01:39:19,075
From gibraltarian to Nile Sea.

999
01:39:19,650 --> 01:39:22,025
We carried the black curse!

1000
01:39:31,385 --> 01:39:35,595
For the blood of
every warrior we sent to Valhalla!

1001
01:39:35,925 --> 01:39:41,005
The north wind will blow
in Osman's land!

1002
01:39:48,585 --> 01:39:50,135
Now...

1003
01:39:51,815 --> 01:39:53,695
For my brother Saga!

1004
01:39:54,955 --> 01:39:56,495
Now!

1005
01:39:56,965 --> 01:40:04,145
For the sake of our warriors we have been
sending to Valhalla for a thousand years!

1006
01:40:06,235 --> 01:40:09,005
It's time to become the black curse!

1007
01:40:44,340 --> 01:40:46,130
May Allah be with you

1008
01:40:46,170 --> 01:40:47,760
Eyvallah my Bey!

1009
01:40:48,150 --> 01:40:49,950
You know what you'll do.

1010
01:40:52,850 --> 01:40:54,610
Bey, someone is approaching!

1011
01:40:58,780 --> 01:41:00,500
That's Kutan.

1012
01:41:03,130 --> 01:41:05,000
Cerkutay Alp is coming, my Bey.

1013
01:41:16,610 --> 01:41:17,910
My Bey!

1014
01:41:19,160 --> 01:41:23,710
They gouged the eyes of the three alps
that Oktem Bey had sent to watch.

1015
01:41:23,710 --> 01:41:25,640
Then they killed them.

1016
01:41:27,390 --> 01:41:31,700
They have been working with all their
power to shed blood, my Bey.

1017
01:41:31,970 --> 01:41:33,670
Traps and ambushes!

1018
01:41:33,850 --> 01:41:36,560
And the treachery even Satan
wouldn't think of!

1019
01:41:37,000 --> 01:41:39,090
All of these are
waiting for us.

1020
01:41:39,500 --> 01:41:41,710
So, we won't keep them waiting long.

1021
01:41:43,000 --> 01:41:45,690
The pits they dug will become their grave.

1022
01:41:46,680 --> 01:41:49,240
They are using our martyrs as a bait...

1023
01:41:49,370 --> 01:41:52,460
...they're waiting for us like a crow, Bey.

1024
01:41:53,310 --> 01:41:54,900
Turgut.

1025
01:41:55,760 --> 01:42:00,050
Show them that Turks won't leave their
martyrs without prayers.

1026
01:42:00,470 --> 01:42:05,880
There is a lot to suffer for that dog
before he dies, Osman Bey.

1027
01:42:07,260 --> 01:42:09,700
They wanted to remove
the emperor from his throne.

1028
01:42:10,400 --> 01:42:12,160
We prevented it.

1029
01:42:12,430 --> 01:42:15,020
We turned Constantinople upside down.

1030
01:42:16,970 --> 01:42:18,820
We ran to the fire with gunpowder.

1031
01:42:20,010 --> 01:42:22,030
And now they're messing with us.

1032
01:42:22,160 --> 01:42:23,880
Axes on their heads...

1033
01:42:24,350 --> 01:42:25,870
Who are these, my Bey?

1034
01:42:25,900 --> 01:42:27,250
What is their problem?

1035
01:42:27,850 --> 01:42:31,180
Those bastards wasted
their years for the nobles.

1036
01:42:31,280 --> 01:42:33,050
They must be careful, Cerkutay.

1037
01:42:33,270 --> 01:42:35,270
It is true what Turgut says.

1038
01:42:35,310 --> 01:42:39,200
There is a group inside
the palace that thinks...

1039
01:42:39,290 --> 01:42:41,900
the Emperor is weak
and helpless against us.

1040
01:42:42,230 --> 01:42:44,750
They are trying to seize
the reins of power...

1041
01:42:45,200 --> 01:42:47,430
and prevent us from advancing to the west.

1042
01:42:47,880 --> 01:42:49,410
But who stirred them up?

1043
01:42:49,550 --> 01:42:51,470
They are not alone.

1044
01:42:51,660 --> 01:42:55,510
If they risk everything to the point of
asking for the support of the Vatican...

1045
01:42:55,570 --> 01:42:57,110
I will never be surprised.

1046
01:42:58,570 --> 01:43:00,940
That's it!

1047
01:43:01,170 --> 01:43:06,160
They set up many traps to drag the emperor
into a war with us, my Bey.

1048
01:43:06,680 --> 01:43:08,170
They won't stop, Cerkutay.

1049
01:43:08,680 --> 01:43:16,310
They will create a lot of sedition to spoil the
peace agreement between us and the Emperor.

1050
01:43:17,260 --> 01:43:19,510
They must take advantage
of any opportunity

1051
01:43:19,510 --> 01:43:22,050
to finish their unfinished
business with the Emperor.

1052
01:43:22,800 --> 01:43:24,670
We have to prepare for a big war...

1053
01:43:24,770 --> 01:43:29,740
that this land has never seen before.

1054
01:43:31,430 --> 01:43:33,970
As if they weren't satisfied with killing
our Alps...

1055
01:43:34,630 --> 01:43:37,110
They also
shamelessly bullied Orhan Bey.

1056
01:43:39,460 --> 01:43:44,570
Now they are setting their
traps and waiting for us.

1057
01:43:44,570 --> 01:43:47,860
The blood of our martyrs has
not yet dried on their hands.

1058
01:43:48,880 --> 01:43:54,400
We will cut off their heads as much as
they broke my son's fingers.

1059
01:43:57,740 --> 01:44:01,770
This calling is from eternity and
will continue forever.

1060
01:44:02,710 --> 01:44:05,510
This call is Allah's call.

1061
01:44:06,860 --> 01:44:11,460
This call is a call to
eliminate the oppressors.

1062
01:44:12,680 --> 01:44:25,480
Allah is the greatest!

1063
01:44:49,085 --> 01:44:51,825
I will clean this black spot
on our forehead.

1064
01:44:52,485 --> 01:44:54,985
I'm going to make this
dog talk, you'll see.

1065
01:44:57,115 --> 01:44:58,665
and who are you?

1066
01:44:59,425 --> 01:45:01,485
I'll beyour death, dog.

1067
01:45:11,065 --> 01:45:12,425
What are you doing
here, Alçiçek?

1068
01:45:12,445 --> 01:45:14,445
Get away from me!

1069
01:45:14,465 --> 01:45:16,975
Let me make this dog speak
for my father's safety!

1070
01:45:17,045 --> 01:45:19,425
The truth can not be reached
by a wrong path!

1071
01:45:19,545 --> 01:45:23,305
What you're doing is punishing you.
Get. out of here before someone sees you.

1072
01:45:24,385 --> 01:45:26,135
Let her come.

1073
01:45:26,565 --> 01:45:27,815
Shut up!

1074
01:45:27,885 --> 01:45:29,885
Come and beat me.

1075
01:45:32,425 --> 01:45:35,565
You are said to be a strong woman.

1076
01:45:39,345 --> 01:45:41,285
I do not leave my
work unfinished.

1077
01:45:41,465 --> 01:45:43,465
I told you to get away from me.

1078
01:45:43,995 --> 01:45:45,655
I told you I'd make this dog talk.

1079
01:45:46,765 --> 01:45:50,855
Come on, let's talk, get over this guy.

1080
01:45:52,285 --> 01:45:54,015
Come on, what are you waiting for?

1081
01:45:54,015 --> 01:45:56,015
I told you to shut up!

1082
01:45:57,015 --> 01:45:58,675
I won't let you do this, Alçiçek.

1083
01:45:58,725 --> 01:46:01,475
Don't you understand
me, commander?

1084
01:46:01,515 --> 01:46:03,365
I told you to get away from me.

1085
01:46:03,515 --> 01:46:05,305
Don't make me hurt you.

1086
01:46:05,765 --> 01:46:08,415
You're basically hurting me
by doing this, Alçiçek.

1087
01:46:08,565 --> 01:46:10,795
This is not the time for stubbornness.

1088
01:46:10,885 --> 01:46:12,915
Get out of here before someone sees you.

1089
01:46:13,115 --> 01:46:15,965
- I told you I'd make him talk.
- Alçiçek.

1090
01:46:23,825 --> 01:46:25,545
Aktemur.

1091
01:46:53,385 --> 01:46:56,585
These pits will be filled
with their corpses.

1092
01:46:58,275 --> 01:47:02,335
They will all shed
blood for the blood of my dear Saga.

1093
01:47:10,275 --> 01:47:13,305
What if Osman doesn't come?

1094
01:47:14,215 --> 01:47:15,715
He will come.

1095
01:47:16,675 --> 01:47:18,985
They do not leave those of them.

1096
01:47:19,765 --> 01:47:24,015
If he doesn't come, we'll go to them.

1097
01:47:25,185 --> 01:47:27,195
I don't want any problem.

1098
01:47:27,255 --> 01:47:32,285
We will surround them when
they fall into the trap.

1099
01:47:33,415 --> 01:47:35,835
I have brought death to this country.

1100
01:47:36,045 --> 01:47:43,215
Like my grandfathers did in the
countries they conquered.

1101
01:47:54,815 --> 01:47:57,645
After Constantinople becomes ours...

1102
01:47:58,635 --> 01:48:00,805
I will conquer the whole world.

1103
01:48:07,785 --> 01:48:10,365
Ignobles.

1104
01:48:11,615 --> 01:48:13,045
Dig ,dig.

1105
01:48:14,505 --> 01:48:16,935
You are digging your own grave.

1106
01:48:23,665 --> 01:48:26,745
Constantinople

1107
01:48:29,985 --> 01:48:33,205
You're wondering why I let you
go, right?

1108
01:48:33,595 --> 01:48:35,475
No, princess.

1109
01:48:35,805 --> 01:48:38,335
I'm the only one you can
trust in the city.

1110
01:48:40,125 --> 01:48:42,755
You were there that day, who
do you suspect?

1111
01:48:43,075 --> 01:48:45,075
I doubt everyone, including you, princess.

1112
01:48:48,865 --> 01:48:51,035
Don't try to fool me
with any answer, Sarkis.

1113
01:48:52,025 --> 01:48:54,115
Where is Prince Kantakuzenos?

1114
01:48:56,725 --> 01:48:59,295
I'm so glad we were all thinking the same.

1115
01:48:59,955 --> 01:49:03,835
If you let me know where he is, I
can do more for you.

1116
01:49:04,925 --> 01:49:07,435
What's the biggest thing
you can do, Sarkis?

1117
01:49:08,205 --> 01:49:09,985
He is a member of the royal family.

1118
01:49:23,995 --> 01:49:27,155
I am so much more than
what you see, Princess.

1119
01:49:27,925 --> 01:49:30,695
And you should be happy
because I serve you.

1120
01:49:31,345 --> 01:49:32,715
This is touching.

1121
01:49:35,805 --> 01:49:37,575
Kantakuzenos.

1122
01:49:37,885 --> 01:49:40,685
He went to our lands
in the East by order of my father.

1123
01:49:43,545 --> 01:49:45,885
Him not being here is
safer for the throne.

1124
01:49:47,205 --> 01:49:52,325
He will attack those who stopped
the attempted coup.

1125
01:49:54,295 --> 01:49:55,855
Turks.

1126
01:50:16,185 --> 01:50:18,765
What are you thinking about that deep,
Aladdin?

1127
01:50:19,325 --> 01:50:20,885
Master Dursun.

1128
01:50:24,355 --> 01:50:25,875
I am very curious.

1129
01:50:27,125 --> 01:50:31,245
I am weak and had
to be a learner.

1130
01:50:31,245 --> 01:50:33,245
But you look so strong...

1131
01:50:34,185 --> 01:50:36,985
Why are you occupied with
science instead of fighting?

1132
01:50:39,355 --> 01:50:40,475
Aladdin.

1133
01:50:42,955 --> 01:50:44,355
Tell me, Aladdin.

1134
01:50:45,215 --> 01:50:48,675
Martyrdom is a pretty high rank, isn't it?

1135
01:50:48,755 --> 01:50:50,075
Of course.

1136
01:50:50,305 --> 01:50:52,155
And I want to be a martyr.

1137
01:50:54,545 --> 01:50:55,635
Now...

1138
01:50:56,085 --> 01:50:59,805
If I told you that our master the Messenger said,

1139
01:50:59,925 --> 01:51:03,755
"The ink of the scholars and
the blood of the martyrs...

1140
01:51:03,755 --> 01:51:06,855
...will be weighed
on the Day of Resurrection...

1141
01:51:06,855 --> 01:51:11,335
...and the ink of the scholars will
outweigh the blood of the martyrs."

1142
01:51:12,215 --> 01:51:14,085
What do you think of this, Aladdin?

1143
01:51:14,085 --> 01:51:17,885
I certainly believe what the Messenger
of Allah says, Master Dursun.

1144
01:51:21,525 --> 01:51:22,975
But I don't understand.

1145
01:51:24,355 --> 01:51:29,815
How is it possible? The ink of the scholars
is higher than the blood of the martyrs?

1146
01:51:32,325 --> 01:51:39,725
This happens when science is for the sake of
Allah, and spreading His name, Alaeddin.

1147
01:51:40,355 --> 01:51:44,505
We are fighting for the sake of
enjoining good and forbidding evil.

1148
01:51:45,365 --> 01:51:52,425
And during the conquests, we tell the verses
of Allah and the Sunnah of His Messenger.

1149
01:51:52,525 --> 01:51:55,755
Can we explain it without knowing
it first, Aladdin?

1150
01:51:57,015 --> 01:51:58,605
We can't do that, Master.

1151
01:52:00,125 --> 01:52:01,715
Of course we can't.

1152
01:52:03,125 --> 01:52:06,905
We will learn in order to inform.

1153
01:52:06,905 --> 01:52:09,385
We must first learn.

1154
01:52:12,275 --> 01:52:14,355
You should know that...

1155
01:52:18,705 --> 01:52:22,355
The more scholars spend ink...

1156
01:52:27,555 --> 01:52:30,705
The less our martyrs lose blood.

1157
01:52:34,355 --> 01:52:36,855
The ink is a shield for the martyrs.

1158
01:52:37,475 --> 01:52:42,005
But what if I want
to be a sword and not a shield?

1159
01:52:47,705 --> 01:52:49,275
Dear Judge...

1160
01:52:54,770 --> 01:52:56,300
Hadrat Judge.

1161
01:52:57,075 --> 01:52:59,665
I complain about
the merchants of Yenişehir.

1162
01:53:00,555 --> 01:53:04,145
They try to harm me
by using religion.

1163
01:53:04,695 --> 01:53:07,345
Stop there, Hatun.
Is this how you enter this room?

1164
01:53:12,425 --> 01:53:14,545
Excuse me, please.

1165
01:53:17,525 --> 01:53:18,865
But...

1166
01:53:19,605 --> 01:53:23,735
They want to pay me after many months.

1167
01:53:24,275 --> 01:53:27,145
And when I wanted to increase the
amount I would take from them...

1168
01:53:27,935 --> 01:53:29,385
...They object to it.

1169
01:53:37,055 --> 01:53:40,505
They say it's "interest"
and that it's forbidden, right?

1170
01:53:43,505 --> 01:53:45,205
And if I don't accept...

1171
01:53:45,445 --> 01:53:47,565
They say they won't take anything from me.

1172
01:53:48,645 --> 01:53:51,415
They say go and trade
in the Christian markets.

1173
01:53:53,045 --> 01:53:55,315
You will give me the names of
those who say so.

1174
01:53:56,115 --> 01:54:00,105
In these lands, everyone can carry out
their business according to the rules...

1175
01:54:00,105 --> 01:54:01,985
...as long as Osman Bey accepts it.

1176
01:54:03,075 --> 01:54:08,635
Those who threaten you will be judged.

1177
01:54:09,865 --> 01:54:14,005
But the thing you want
from the merchants is interest.

1178
01:54:15,175 --> 01:54:16,705
And our messenger of Allah...

1179
01:54:17,055 --> 01:54:22,775
...cursed the one who pays interest and
takes it and bears witness to it

1180
01:54:23,655 --> 01:54:28,355
Islam permitted trading
and prohibited interest.

1181
01:54:30,155 --> 01:54:35,455
So in this case, they will pay for
the fabrics they took in cash.

1182
01:54:41,755 --> 01:54:45,945
Honest merchants may come to you
but they don't have instant money.

1183
01:54:46,985 --> 01:54:51,725
There must be
a solution that makes everyone happy.

1184
01:54:53,365 --> 01:54:56,125
You will show your profit
when you sell your goods

1185
01:54:57,245 --> 01:55:00,645
And if the capital of your merchandise
increases after several months...

1186
01:55:01,175 --> 01:55:03,425
You will take your
profits from the customer.

1187
01:55:04,455 --> 01:55:06,215
This is Caiz (acceptable by the religion).

1188
01:55:29,805 --> 01:55:31,805
My Master Dursun is telling the truth

1189
01:55:32,565 --> 01:55:35,675
But, but that is not the issue.

1190
01:55:37,395 --> 01:55:39,165
Of course, science is important.

1191
01:55:39,755 --> 01:55:42,995
My dad doesn't give me
assignments because he doesn't trust me.

1192
01:55:42,995 --> 01:55:45,555
I know I'm not like my brother.

1193
01:56:00,245 --> 01:56:02,255
You have fallen into my hands now, Aladdin

1194
01:56:08,835 --> 01:56:10,225
Come on.

1195
01:56:13,765 --> 01:56:15,565
Enter that street!

1196
01:56:16,575 --> 01:56:19,575
Your hell is waiting for you!

1197
01:56:49,355 --> 01:56:51,435
Thieves! Who are you?

1198
01:56:51,555 --> 01:56:53,055
That's a trap!

1199
01:57:07,595 --> 01:57:09,315
I'm here, my Bey!

1200
01:57:13,105 --> 01:57:14,805
My Bey, call for help!

1201
01:57:16,055 --> 01:57:17,595
Run my Bey!

1202
01:57:34,145 --> 01:57:35,715
Are you okay?

1203
01:57:53,695 --> 01:57:55,045
My Bey!

1204
01:58:25,245 --> 01:58:26,745
They are approaching.

1205
01:58:27,935 --> 01:58:29,245
Let them.

1206
01:58:30,215 --> 01:58:32,535
Hell is waiting for them.

1207
01:58:47,095 --> 01:58:48,805
What is happening?

1208
02:00:34,045 --> 02:00:35,635
Osman.

1209
02:00:57,235 --> 02:00:58,745
Osman.

1210
02:01:01,055 --> 02:01:02,645
You kill our alps.

1211
02:01:03,655 --> 02:01:05,935
You don't give us our funerals.

1212
02:01:06,355 --> 02:01:08,165
That's true.

1213
02:01:08,855 --> 02:01:10,865
Because you are the one I speak to.

1214
02:01:11,965 --> 02:01:16,495
What's more, in order to take our martyrs,
you set a trap for us.

1215
02:01:18,895 --> 02:01:20,945
You don't want peace.

1216
02:01:21,735 --> 02:01:23,745
Your intention is to break us.

1217
02:01:24,375 --> 02:01:26,125
I don't trust my enemy.

1218
02:01:27,505 --> 02:01:29,285
This is only a precaution.

1219
02:01:29,425 --> 02:01:31,015
Alright then.

1220
02:01:31,395 --> 02:01:33,455
We ignore it.

1221
02:01:36,265 --> 02:01:38,125
Now we will take our martyrs.

1222
02:01:39,695 --> 02:01:42,755
Come and take them if you can, Osman!

1223
02:01:43,995 --> 02:01:46,075
We have already taken our martyrs.

1224
02:01:50,540 --> 02:01:53,299
Sogut.

1225
02:02:07,565 --> 02:02:08,915
Oh...

1226
02:02:11,575 --> 02:02:13,285
The secret has been exposed.

1227
02:02:14,725 --> 02:02:16,455
The way is seen.

1228
02:02:18,735 --> 02:02:20,555
Thins are going crazy in Yenisehir.

1229
02:02:21,095 --> 02:02:22,605
Crazy as hell.

1230
02:02:23,615 --> 02:02:25,165
Crazy as hell.

1231
02:02:27,340 --> 02:02:29,680
- Where are you going?
- The road is exposed.

1232
02:02:29,940 --> 02:02:31,810
Yenişehir is calling us!

1233
02:02:31,840 --> 02:02:33,730
We are going to Yenişehir!

1234
02:02:52,490 --> 02:02:54,990
"We belong to Allah
and to Him we shall return"

1235
02:02:55,940 --> 02:02:57,250
Amen.

1236
02:02:58,520 --> 02:03:00,660
Your blood will not be in vain,
my brothers.

1237
02:03:02,400 --> 02:03:06,450
It is forbidden for us to breathe
until we avenge!

1238
02:03:10,770 --> 02:03:12,360
Let's act alps!

1239
02:03:26,705 --> 02:03:29,765
This food is tasteless,
it tastes like barley!

1240
02:03:34,395 --> 02:03:36,535
Where are you, Cerkutay?

1241
02:03:36,935 --> 02:03:39,225
Are you full or hungry?

1242
02:03:45,305 --> 02:03:47,535
Shall I, Aunt Ulgen, taste it?

1243
02:03:47,535 --> 02:03:49,535
Taste it my daughter.

1244
02:03:50,275 --> 02:03:52,475
But something happened to me.

1245
02:03:53,105 --> 02:03:55,625
There is no taste for this food,
my dear Fatima.

1246
02:03:59,455 --> 02:04:01,735
It's too salty, Aunt Ulgen!

1247
02:04:02,595 --> 02:04:03,895
What?

1248
02:04:08,595 --> 02:04:12,395
What salt are you talking about?
This is just tasteless.

1249
02:04:21,135 --> 02:04:22,875
What is happening to me?

1250
02:04:28,825 --> 02:04:31,125
I can no longer taste the food!

1251
02:04:35,135 --> 02:04:37,165
Of course, this is because of
the absence of Cerkutay!

1252
02:04:37,595 --> 02:04:41,675
Oh Cerkutay! There is no taste in
this mansion when you are absent

1253
02:04:45,105 --> 02:04:46,635
Ulgen!

1254
02:04:47,205 --> 02:04:49,255
Have you seen Aladdin?

1255
02:04:49,255 --> 02:04:51,615
I haven't seen him, Bala Hatun,
what's wrong?

1256
02:04:52,565 --> 02:04:55,195
Allah Allah!
Where is this boy?

1257
02:04:55,595 --> 02:04:57,335
He must have gone to Master Dursun.

1258
02:04:57,335 --> 02:04:59,335
He should have come back by now.

1259
02:05:01,965 --> 02:05:03,495
Bala!

1260
02:05:04,855 --> 02:05:06,425
Bala!

1261
02:05:11,195 --> 02:05:12,735
Bala!

1262
02:05:27,425 --> 02:05:29,975
Our martyrs are with us, for sure.

1263
02:05:31,565 --> 02:05:33,155
Osman Bey.

1264
02:05:37,795 --> 02:05:40,855
As if you didn't already
give me a reason for war

1265
02:05:40,855 --> 02:05:44,855
The last thing you will hear
will be the trumpets of doomsday!

1266
02:05:45,195 --> 02:05:50,365
We'll be resurrected on the Day of Resurrection
under the banner of the Messenger of Allah.

1267
02:05:51,195 --> 02:05:55,725
But it is you
who have to fear the doomsday.

1268
02:06:09,500 --> 02:06:11,040
Alps!

1269
02:06:12,270 --> 02:06:13,630
Bala Hatun.

1270
02:06:13,630 --> 02:06:14,880
What happened?

1271
02:06:14,980 --> 02:06:16,680
Who attacked you?

1272
02:06:17,150 --> 02:06:19,430
They kidnapped Alaeddin Bey.

1273
02:06:19,430 --> 02:06:20,480
What?

1274
02:06:20,480 --> 02:06:22,480
We couldn't save him.

1275
02:06:23,470 --> 02:06:25,470
We couldn't save him.

1276
02:06:26,950 --> 02:06:28,280
Son!

1277
02:06:29,640 --> 02:06:31,200
Alps!

1278
02:06:31,200 --> 02:06:34,570
Take him to the healing room
right now, come on!

1279
02:06:37,130 --> 02:06:41,300
Sisters, close all the doors of
Yenişehir, no one will leave!

1280
02:06:41,300 --> 02:06:42,400
Come on!

1281
02:06:42,400 --> 02:06:45,600
Alps, find me a trace of my son!

1282
02:06:48,240 --> 02:06:50,950
I don't get involved in a war
that has already begun.

1283
02:06:51,350 --> 02:06:53,140
I start the war.

1284
02:06:55,490 --> 02:06:57,610
This is your last chance.

1285
02:06:59,040 --> 02:07:00,550
The court will be held.

1286
02:07:01,750 --> 02:07:03,750
The truth will be revealed.

1287
02:07:05,150 --> 02:07:07,520
Blood don't need blood in return.

1288
02:07:07,520 --> 02:07:09,520
Blood needs blood, Osman.

1289
02:07:10,040 --> 02:07:12,860
Blood needs blood!

1290
02:07:17,490 --> 02:07:18,640
Alright then.

1291
02:07:19,490 --> 02:07:23,370
Your court will be held on the battlefield.

1292
02:07:53,920 --> 02:07:55,460
I trust you with my gift.

1293
02:07:55,460 --> 02:07:56,850
Take a good care of him.

1294
02:07:56,850 --> 02:07:58,850
We will hand him over
to his owner, madam.

1295
02:08:14,160 --> 02:08:18,140
By order of Bala Hatun, close the doors!

1296
02:08:20,860 --> 02:08:22,390
Alaeddin!

1297
02:08:22,690 --> 02:08:24,490
Where are you, baby?

1298
02:08:24,490 --> 02:08:26,350
Where are you son?

1299
02:08:28,320 --> 02:08:29,890
Alaeddin!

1300
02:08:30,090 --> 02:08:33,350
Bala, we'll find your son.

1301
02:08:33,640 --> 02:08:34,940
Ayse!

1302
02:08:34,940 --> 02:08:36,940
We will find him, Bala.

1303
02:08:39,140 --> 02:08:40,660
Bala Hatun!

1304
02:08:42,260 --> 02:08:45,100
We found Alaeddin Bey's hat and
his book, they're bloody.

1305
02:09:14,580 --> 02:09:16,280
My Alaeddin!

1306
02:10:13,520 --> 02:10:15,520
I will kill you with your weapon.

1307
02:10:16,750 --> 02:10:19,350
My axe is like Thor's hammer.

1308
02:10:19,380 --> 02:10:21,390
No one who doesn't deserve can carry it.

1309
02:10:21,390 --> 02:10:23,390
It's time for your trial.

1310
02:10:23,390 --> 02:10:24,950
Come to me now.

1311
02:10:54,380 --> 02:10:55,890
Osman Bey!

1312
02:10:57,040 --> 02:10:58,350
Stop!

1313
02:10:59,920 --> 02:11:01,960
I am here in the name of the emperor.

1314
02:11:03,640 --> 02:11:06,220
You are fighting the wrong enemy.

1315
02:11:23,750 --> 02:11:26,340
...I don't know whom you work with,
but...

1316
02:11:28,640 --> 02:11:30,720
You won't leave here empty-handed.

1317
02:11:35,010 --> 02:11:37,060
Let me explain it to you

1318
02:11:37,060 --> 02:11:42,620
The risen sword shall not lower
without blood on it.

1319
02:11:49,270 --> 02:12:03,640
Please contact us for any inquiries
turkision@gmail.com